{"parentUuid":"eb096f9c-dc30-4901-848a-483989636200","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01MsVrMfXZ9Y2y6EvHWUBW4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed and verified. Here's the root cause and fix:\n\n**Bug:** `entire judge run <repo>` resolved the brain dir from its *own* plugin data dir — `env.PluginDataDir` is `…/data/judge` when dispatched as `entire judge`, so it looked in `…/data/judge/repos/…`. But `entire brain refresh` writes to the sibling `…/data/brain/repos/…`. Mismatch → `brain_missing`.\n\n**Fix** (`internal/cli/env.go`): `resolveBrainStorage` now searches the **brain plugin's** data dir first (the sibling `…/data/brain`, where `entire brain` writes — Thomas's exact path), then falls back to judge's own dir (where `entire judge add` writes), so both flows work. The `brain_missing` error now points at the brain-plugin path. Added `TestResolveBrainStorageFindsBrainPluginDir` (Thomas's case), the `judge add` fallback, the missing-brain case, and `TestBrainDataDirs`. `go vet`, full `go test ./...`, and `-race` all green.\n\nThere are now **two changesets ready**, both uncommitted/unpushed:\n- **entire-brain** — the dash TUI + search + `add` (staged, with the 4 audit fixes; this is the push you started, authorized to `claude/brain-dash-tui`).\n- **entire-judge** — this brain-path fix (on `main`, so it needs a branch)."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_read_input_tokens":453660,"output_tokens":3097,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1147,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3097,"cache_read_input_tokens":453660,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_to