{"parentUuid":"2f6e84b4-9f03-4cf0-b972-dd803849b98d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01H61KctfqcoL8fCgnQrcXzu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RxfNChTLu2SEqP4xRwxNHd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain\necho \"=== branch + staged set ===\"; git branch --show-current; git diff --cached --name-status\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfeat(dash): interactive brain dashboard TUI with search and `add`\n\nAdd `entire brain dash`, a gh-dash-style two-pane terminal dashboard for\nexploring a built brain: a Home status/coverage tab plus Facts, Sessions,\nHistory, Semantic, and Search tabs, each with a per-entry detail page. It is\nread-only and no-egress — it only formats data the brain already stores.\n\n- internal/tui: new rendering package (themes, tabs, table, detail, keys,\n  fuzzy filter, viewport scroll, mouse, OSC 8 source links). Pure view models;\n  no file IO of its own.\n- internal/cli/dash.go: assembles the snapshot from existing loaders (status,\n  facts, sessions, history index, semantic snapshot) and wires the `s` search\n  key to the same retrieval as `entire brain search` (lexical, read-only).\n- internal/cli/add.go: `entire brain add <repo-url>` clones a repo, fetches its\n  Entire history, and builds the brain via refresh, so no manual clone is needed.\n\nTests cover the row/detail builders, theme/tab parsing, the async search flow,\nfull tab cycling, path containment, and the add URL guards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1\necho \"=== push ===\"; git push -u origin claude/brain-dash-tui 2>&1 | tail -6","description":"Commit and push entire-brain dash branch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":741,"cache_read_input_tokens":460999,"output_tokens":979,"