{"parentUuid":"7d3be4c6-a6d7-442c-983a-e70cec523fee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01ByDUtFY4wGxPTnc6DLDE1j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reviewed all 5 Copilot comments — each was legitimate, and all are now fixed and pushed (commit `de3f8549`):\n\n| # | Copilot comment | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `add` returns exit 0 even when the brain **build fails** → scripts treat failure as success | Now returns a non-zero `brain_build_failed` error (clone kept on disk, manual-build guidance printed) |\n| 2 | `--tab` help omits `search` | Added `search` to the flag help |\n| 3 | `unknown_tab` error omits `search` | Added `search` to the error message |\n| 4 | Submitting a search keeps search mode open → repeated Enter enqueues overlapping searches, results can apply **out of order** | Exit search mode immediately on submit + drop stale async results via an in-flight `pendingQuery` guard |\n| 5 | Semantic `FilePath` → `o`-open target wasn't path-validated → a **tampered snapshot** could open files outside the repo | Routed it through the shared containment helper (`brainRelPath` → generalized to `containedPath`, now used for both brain- and repo-relative paths) |\n\nAdded a regression test (`TestSearchExitsModeOnSubmitAndDropsStale`) for #4; the containment + rename are covered by the existing path tests. Locally green: `gofmt -s`, `go build`, `go vet`, full `cli`+`tui` tests, and `-race`.\n\nCI is re-running on the new commit now. Want me to confirm it goes green again, or is that enough?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":882,"cache_read_input_tokens":522020,"output_tokens":884,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":882,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens