{"parentUuid":"d01352ba-d2a2-4905-81d7-dcc1c77e9278","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014U3Eq3MygXr7BYqNnguTGu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016x94hVaGJgA8e4b8agQRso","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain\necho \"=== PR #44 overview ===\"\ngh pr view 44 --json number,title,state,headRefName,baseRefName,author,additions,deletions,body -q '{number,title,state,head:.headRefName,base:.baseRefName,author:.author.login,additions,deletions}' 2>&1 | head\necho \"\"\necho \"=== body (first 1500 chars) ===\"\ngh pr view 44 --json body -q .body 2>&1 | head -c 1500\necho \"\"\necho \"=== changed files ===\"\ngh pr diff 44 --name-only 2>&1 | head -60","description":"Fetch PR #44 metadata and changed files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":958,"cache_read_input_tokens":522902,"output_tokens":913,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":958,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":913,"cache_read_input_tokens":522902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":958,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":958},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cc98ynCxPfX5rkGDKuUxG","type":"assistant","uuid":"1170a5e0-bc0e-4221-bc75-6e4e3f2d9b3f","timestamp":"2026-06-17T16:21:38.912Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"1170a5e0-bc0e-4221-bc75-6e4e3f2d9b3f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e994dde8-5879-4b7d-b7a3-329a07d36f1c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016x94hVaGJgA8e4b8agQRso","type":"tool_result","content":"=== PR #44 overview ===\n{\"additions\":8430,\"author\":\"ashtom\",\"base\":\"claude/patterns-phase0-reinforcement\",\"deletions\":348,\"head\":\"claude/patterns-v2-corpus\",\"number\":44,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"patterns v2: rebuildable SQLite pattern corpus (stacked on #43)\"}\n\n=== body (first 1500 chars) ===\nImplements `docs/pattern_v2.md` end-to-end: a clean-room, Entire-Brain-native pattern **corpus** (`patterns/corpus.sqlite`) that improves the *whole* brain — refresh, patterns, brief, overview, query/get, review, handoff, MCP, and workspaces — with skill formation as one downstream consumer. Stacked on #43; reuses that branch's deterministic, token-free extraction + redaction. **No new model calls on the refresh/watch path.**\n\n## What's new (the 8-priority completion)\n\n**P1 — `patterns` reads the V2 corpus.** The public listing (+`--json`, `--type task|procedure|risk|practice|theme`, `--scope`) reads `patterns`/`pattern_evidence`/`dossiers`: type, scope, strength, support, dossier/verifier state, top anchor, id. Rejected dossiers suppressed; legacy JSON is fallback only.\n\n**P2 — workspaces are first-class V2.** `buildWorkspacePatternCorpus` aggregates member-repo corpora (not merged JSON) into a workspace corpus: `scope='workspace'`, `n_repos>=2`, per-repo breakdown (`workspace_pattern_repos`), member anchors, stable ids. Only redacted anchor pointers cross into the workspace store. `workspace patterns <name>`, `workspace refresh`, and `workspace get <ws> <repo-key>/pattern:<id>` all wired.\n\n**P3 — the missing tables, implemented.** `episode_symbols` (semantic graph), `episode_commits` (local `[branch hash]` only, no network), `synapses` (explanation edges: pattern→evidence→fact/file/symbol/commit, workspace→repo), `themes` table, and a run-history surface (`p\n=== changed files ===\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/go-test-internal-cli-radar.jsonl\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/radar-tool-audit-report.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/radar-tool-audit-report.md\ndocs/pattern_v2.md\ninternal/cli/agent_surface.go\ninternal/cli/handoff.go\ninternal/cli/mcp.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_candidates.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_candidates_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_corpus.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_corpus_enrich.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_corpus_enrich_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_corpus_links.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_corpus_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_deep.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_deep_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_dossier.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_dossier_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_links_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_list_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_p6_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_quality_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_runs.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_skill_bridge.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_skill_bridge_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_surface.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_surface_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_themes.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_themes_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_verify.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_verify_test.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_workspace.go\ninternal/cli/pattern_workspace_test.go\ninternal/cli/patterns_cmd.go\ninternal/cli/redaction.go\ninternal/cli/refresh.go\ninternal/cli/regression.go\ninternal/cli/retrieve.go\ninternal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go\ninternal/cli/review_fixes_test.go\ninternal/cli/skill_cmd.go\ninternal/cli/workspace.go\ninternal/cli/workspace_patterns.go","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cebcf8cb-19c2-40bf-91c6-6a8c2de5eb36","timestamp":"2026-06-17T16:21:40.692Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== PR #44 overview ===\n{\"additions\":8430,\"author\":\"ashtom\",\"base\":\"claude/patterns-phase0-reinforcement\",\"deletions\":348,\"head\":\"claude/patterns-v2-corpus\",\"number\":44,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"patterns v2: rebuildable SQLite pattern corpus (stacked on #43)\"}\n\n=== body (first 1500 chars) ===\nImplements `docs/pattern_v2.md` end-to-end: a clean-room, Entire-Brain-native pattern **corpus** (`patterns/corpus.sqlite`) that improves the *whole* brain — refresh, patterns, brief, overview, query/get, review, handoff, MCP, and workspaces — with skill formation as one downstream consumer. Stacked on #43; reuses that branch's deterministic, token-free extraction + redaction. **No new model calls on the refresh/watch path.**\n\n## What's new (the 8-priority completion)\n\n**P1 — `patterns` reads the V2 corpus.** The public listing (+`--json`, `--type task|procedure|risk|practice|theme`, `--scope`) reads `patterns`/`pattern_evidence`/`dossiers`: type, scope, strength, support, dossier/verifier state, top anchor, id. Rejected dossiers suppressed; legacy JSON is fallback only.\n\n**P2 — workspaces are first-class V2.** `buildWorkspacePatternCorpus` aggregates member-repo corpora (not merged JSON) into a workspace corpus: `scope='workspace'`, `n_repos>=2`, per-repo breakdown (`workspace_pattern_repos`), member anchors, stable ids. Only redacted anchor pointers cross into the workspace store. `workspace patterns <name>`, `workspace refresh`, and `workspace get <ws> <repo-key>/pattern:<id>` all wired.\n\n**P3 — the missing tables, implemented.** `episode_symbols` (semantic graph), `episode_commits` (local `[branch hash]` only, no network), `synapses` (explanation edges: pattern→evidence→fact/file/symbol/commit, workspace→repo), `themes` table, and a run-history surface (`p\n=== changed files ===\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/go-test-internal-cli-radar.jsonl\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/manifest.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/radar-tool-audit-report.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/radar-tool/radar-tool-audit-report.md\ndocs/pattern_v2.md\ninternal/cli/agent_surface.go\n