{"parentUuid":"8661fb16-1bfd-4314-8039-5abe528f1cc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Cmeb23QMkgZRZgYbDjG3zG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Skill identification lives under `entire brain patterns skills` (list) and `patterns skills form` (synthesize). Let me read the gist of the design doc and the skill command, and kick off a build:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5348,"cache_read_input_tokens":528194,"output_tokens":766,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5348,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":528194,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5348,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5348},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cc993NfDpFkNhvMf1XQfB","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef163780-1413-4fda-b18a-fba23515e937","timestamp":"2026-06-17T16:22:26.756Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/patterns-v2-corpus","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"ef163780-1413-4fda-b18a-fba23515e937","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Cmeb23QMkgZRZgYbDjG3zG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017SzL4zRU9mRpokU1hRvGbM","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/pattern_v2.md","limit":115},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5348,"cache_read_input_tokens":528194,"output_tokens":766,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5348,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":528194,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5348,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5348},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cc993NfDpFkNhvMf1XQfB","type":"assistant","uuid":"aef92247-b2e4-4723-b7b7-25aac36d609b","timestamp":"2026-06-17T16:22:26.972Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/patterns-v2-corpus","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"aef92247-b2e4-4723-b7b7-25aac36d609b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e994dde8-5879-4b7d-b7a3-329a07d36f1c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017SzL4zRU9mRpokU1hRvGbM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Entire Brain V2 Pattern Corpus Plan\n2\t\n3\t## Objective\n4\t\n5\tImplement a clean-room, Entire Brain native pattern-corpus layer that improves\n6\tthe whole brain: `brief`, `query`, `overview`, `review`, MCP, handoff,\n7\tworkspaces, and optional skill formation.\n8\t\n9\tDo not design this as a standalone skill extractor. Skill formation is one\n10\tdownstream consumer. The core product goal is better repository memory, task\n11\tguidance, cross-repo awareness, provenance, and drift detection.\n12\t\n13\tDo not copy naming, schema, commands, or docs from any external implementation.\n14\tUse only Entire Brain's existing concepts: sessions, history, facts, docs,\n15\tsemantic graph, workspaces, refresh, brief, query, review, MCP, and local\n16\tstorage.\n17\t\n18\tThis plan assumes the Phase 0 pattern-consolidation work may already exist on\n19\tthe implementation branch. If it has not landed yet, treat compatible readable\n20\tpattern artifacts and skill-memory behavior as prerequisites to preserve or\n21\tfold into this work, not as requirements to duplicate.\n22\t\n23\t## Vocabulary\n24\t\n25\tUse brain-themed internal terms.\n26\t\n27\t| Term | Meaning |\n28\t| --- | --- |\n29\t| Episode | One user request, the agent work that followed, and the next feedback signal. |\n30\t| Pattern | Recurring work, judgment, risk, validation habit, or cross-repo behavior. |\n31\t| Consolidation | Evidence-backed summary of a recurring pattern. |\n32\t| Dossier | Stored consolidation artifact: trigger, steps, variants, verification, failure modes, refs, verifier result. |\n33\t| Synapse | Internal-only weighted evidence edge connecting brain records. |\n34\t| Decision | User or system state about a pattern or consolidation, such as accepted, declined, stale, edited, missing, or suppressed. |\n35\t\n36\t`Synapse` must not be exposed as a CLI command or user-facing concept. It is an\n37\tinternal data model for explainable scoring, provenance, and drift.\n38\t\n39\tExample synapse:\n40\t\n41\t```json\n42\t{\n43\t  \"from_id\": \"episode:abc\",\n44\t  \"to_id\": \"fact:def\",\n45\t  \"kind\": \"supports\",\n46\t  \"weight\": 0.82,\n47\t  \"source_anchor\": \"sessions/main/x.jsonl:123\"\n48\t}\n49\t```\n50\t\n51\tInitial synapse kinds:\n52\t\n53\t- `mentions`\n54\t- `supports`\n55\t- `reinforces`\n56\t- `contradicts`\n57\t- `varies`\n58\t- `derived_from`\n59\t- `affects`\n60\t- `validated_by`\n61\t- `failed_by`\n62\t\n63\t## Constraints\n64\t\n65\t- Keep public commands aligned to user jobs.\n66\t- Do not introduce hidden commands for this work.\n67\t- Do not require hosted model calls in `refresh`.\n68\t- Keep generated artifacts local and inspectable.\n69\t- Preserve workspace support as a first-class requirement.\n70\t- Preserve existing readable NDJSON exports where useful.\n71\t- Add richer internal indexing only behind existing command surfaces.\n72\t- Redact secrets before any CLI, JSON, MCP, agent, cache, or draft egress.\n73\t- Preserve the local-only boundary: no implicit network operations, no remote\n74\t  service, and MCP remains stdio-only.\n75\t- Honor strict no-egress mode and existing agent-gating behavior.\n76\t\n77\t## Design Considerations\n78\t\n79\tThe expected upside is broad: better task packets, better retrieval context,\n80\tbetter diff-less review, better workspace awareness, better provenance, and more\n81\treliable optional skill formation. Treat those upsides as hypotheses to prove,\n82\tnot assumptions.\n83\t\n84\tFor each implementation phase, evaluate outcomes against existing Entire Brain\n85\tfeatures. The target is not \"more pattern data\"; the target is better answers\n86\twithout regressing refresh, watch, retrieval, workspace, local-only, or\n87\tinspectability guarantees.\n88\t\n89\tEvaluate and document these tradeoffs:\n90\t\n91\t- **Refresh and watch cost:** Pattern corpus refresh should be incremental,\n92\t  bounded, deterministic, and token-free. A pattern-corpus failure should not\n93\t  make the normal brain unusable by default. Decide which failures should be\n94\t  warnings in `refresh` and which should fail an explicit `patterns refresh`.\n95\t- **Retrieval noise:** Pattern, episode, and consolidation records may improve\n96\t  `query`/`brief`, but they may also crowd out facts/history/docs. Prove that\n97\t  relevance improves or stays neutral before adding them to default retrieval.\n98\t- **Agent boundaries:** Optional agent-assisted consolidation must have an\n99\t  explicit command or flag boundary. It must not run from plain `refresh`,\n100\t  `watch`, `brief`, `query`, MCP read tools, or workspace refresh.\n101\t- **Workspace storage boundaries:** Workspace aggregation should store\n102\t  repo-qualified references, summaries, ids, and breakdowns. It must not copy\n103\t  raw member transcripts or generated member brain records into another repo's\n104\t  brain.\n105\t- **User-state safety:** Rebuildable corpus data and user decisions must have a\n106\t  hard separation. Deleting or rebuilding `patterns/corpus.sqlite` must not\n107\t  delete accepted, declined, suppressed, edited, or missing-state decisions.\n108\t- **Optional source layers:** Semantic graph and durable facts should enrich the\n109\t  corpus when present. Missing semantic/fact layers must degrade gracefully and\n110\t  must never trigger distillation.\n111\t- **Branch and freshness scope:** Durable facts are branch-scoped, semantic data\n112\t  has freshness state, and history/docs are indexed snapshots. Pattern records\n113\t  must preserve those scopes instead of flattening them into one global truth.\n114\t- **Raw text and secrets:** Prefer redacted display text plus source anchors in\n115\t  the corpus. Raw retained transcript content should remain in the existing"}]},"uuid":"d515d0fb-f192-4403-bebd-6356f0fd1e81","timestamp":"2026-06-17T16:22:27.013Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/pattern_v2.md","content":"# Entire Brain V2 Pattern Corpus Plan\n\n## Objective\n\nImplement a clean-room, Entire Brain native pattern-corpus layer that improves\nthe whole brain: `brief`, `query`, `overview`, `review`, MCP, handoff,\nworkspaces, and optional skill formation.\n\nDo not design this as a standalone skill extractor. Skill formation is one\ndownstream consumer. The core product goal is better repository memory, task\nguidance, cross-repo awareness, provenance, and drift detection.\n\nDo not copy naming, schema, commands, or docs from any external implementation.\nUse only Entire Brain's existing concepts: sessions, history, facts, docs,\nsemantic graph, workspaces, refresh, brief, query, review, MCP, and local\nstorage.\n\nThis plan assumes the Phase 0 pattern-consolidation work may already exist on\nthe implementation branch. If it has not landed yet, treat compatible readable\npattern artifacts and skill-memory behavior as prerequisites to preserve or\nfold into this work, not as requirements to duplicate.\n\n## Vocabulary\n\nUse brain-themed internal terms.\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| Episode | One user request, the agent work that followed, and the next feedback signal. |\n| Pattern | Recurring work, judgment, risk, validation habit, or cross-repo behavior. |\n| Consolidation | Evidence-backed summary of a recurring pattern. |\n| Dossier | Stored consolidation artifact: trigger, steps, variants, verification, failure modes, refs, verifier result. |\n| Synapse | Internal-only weighted evidence edge connecting brain records. |\n| Decision | User or system state about a pattern or consolidation, such as accepted, declined, stale, edited, missing, or suppressed. |\n\n`Synapse` must not be exposed as a CLI command or user-facing concept. It is an\ninternal data model for explainable scoring, provenance, and drift.\n\nExample synapse:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"from_id\": \"episode:abc\",\n  \"to_id\": \"fact:def\",\n  \"kind\": \"supports\",\n  \"weight\": 0.82,\n  \"source_anchor\": \"sessions/main/x.jsonl:123\"\n}\n```\n\nInitial synapse kinds:\n\n- `mentions`\n- `supports`\n- `reinforces`\n- `contradicts`\n- `varies`\n- `derived_from`\n- `affects`\n- `validated_by`\n- `failed_by`\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Keep public commands aligned to user jobs.\n- Do not introduce hidden commands for this work.\n- Do not require hosted model calls in `refresh`.\n- Keep generated artifacts local and inspectable.\n- Preserve workspace support as a first-class requirement.\n- Preserve existing readable NDJSON exports where useful.\n- Add richer internal indexing only behind existing command surfaces.\n- Redact secrets before any CLI, JSON, MCP, agent, cache, or draft egress.\n- Preserve the local-only boundary: no implicit network operations, no remote\n  service, and MCP remains stdio-only.\n- Honor strict no-egress mode and existing agent-gating behavior.\n\n## Design Considerations\n\nThe expected upside is broad: better task packets, better retrieval context,\nbetter diff-less review, better workspace awareness, better provenance, and more\nreliable optional skill formation. Treat those upsides as hypotheses to prove,\nnot assumptions.\n\nFor each implementation phase, evaluate outcomes against existing Entire Brain\nfeatures. The target is not \"more pattern data\"; the target is better answers\nwithout regressing refresh, watch, retrieval, workspace, local-only, or\ninspectability guarantees.\n\nEvaluate and document these tradeoffs:\n\n- **Refresh and watch cost:** Pattern corpus refresh should be incremental,\n  bounded, deterministic, and token-free. A pattern-corpus failure should not\n  make the normal brain unusable by default. Decide which failures should be\n  warnings in `refresh` and which should fail an explicit `patterns refresh`.\n- **Retrieval noise:** Pattern, episode, and consolidation records may improve\n  `query`/`brief`, but they may also crowd out facts/history/docs. Prove that\n  relevance improves or stays neutral before adding them to default retrieval.\n- **Agent boundaries:** Optional agent-assisted consolidation must have an\n  explicit command or flag boundary. It must not run from plain `refresh`,\n  `watch`, `brief`, `query`, MCP read tools, or workspace refresh.\n- **Workspace storage boundaries:** Workspace aggregation should store\n  repo-qualified references, summaries, ids, and breakdowns. It must not copy\n  raw member transcripts or generated member brain records into another repo's\n  brain.\n- **User-state safety:** Rebuildable corpus data and user decisions must have a\n  hard separation. Deleting or rebuilding `patterns/corpus.sqlite` must not\n  delete accepted, declined, suppressed, edited, or missing-state decisions.\n- **Optional source layers:** Semantic graph and durable facts should enrich the\n  corpus when present. Missing semantic/fact layers must degrade gracefully and\n  must never trigger distillation.\n- **Branch and freshness scope:** Durable facts are branch-scoped, semantic data\n  has freshness state, and history/docs are indexed snapshots. Pattern records\n  must preserve those scopes instead of flattening them into one global truth.\n- **Raw text and secrets:** Prefer redacted display text plus source anchors in\n  the corpus. Raw retained transcript content should remain in the existing","numLines":115,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1128}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aef92247-b2e4-4723-b7b7-25aac36d609b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/patterns-v2-corpus","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
