{"parentUuid":"ee9fe902-faf8-4b0f-b377-012fb11a1453","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e994dde8-5879-4b7d-b7a3-329a07d36f1c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CR5eUQQmtgWfGyu5fWaSRm","type":"tool_result","content":"Switched to branch 'claude/brain-dash-tui'\nYour branch is up to date with 'origin/claude/brain-dash-tui'.\nclaude/brain-dash-tui","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8ba3bcf0-4627-48e0-9132-b40bd7c64c78","timestamp":"2026-06-17T16:25:59.056Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Switched to branch 'claude/brain-dash-tui'\nYour branch is up to date with 'origin/claude/brain-dash-tui'.\nclaude/brain-dash-tui","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee9fe902-faf8-4b0f-b377-012fb11a1453","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/patterns-v2-corpus","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"8ba3bcf0-4627-48e0-9132-b40bd7c64c78","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YaEW4Wos5vtYkwt1nB86sE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I tried PR #44 end-to-end against this repo's brain. Here's the verdict.\n\n## How it works\n`pattern_v2.md` is a corpus design (not a standalone skill extractor) — skill formation is one downstream consumer. The skill surface is:\n- `entire brain patterns skills` — lists recurring **task candidates** (deterministic, token-free)\n- `entire brain patterns skills form <id>` — synthesizes a `SKILL.md` via an agent, evidence-first preview, writes only with `--yes`, rejects `NOT_A_SKILL`\n\n## What works really well ✅\n`patterns refresh` built the corpus in **~5s, token-free/deterministic**: 871 episodes, 756 patterns, 2 dossiers, 514 symbol links, 190 commits, 3940 synapses. The `patterns` listing is genuinely useful — it surfaced real, anchored practices from my sessions: `validation_loop` (79 eps, 37↑), `no_egress_constraint`, `review_request`, `read_only_diagnosis`, `handoff_resume`, plus git procedures (`git status ▷ git diff`). That's the \"improve the whole brain\" goal landing.\n\n## The rough edge: `patterns skills` returns **nothing** on an active brain\n`no task candidates` — even though the corpus has 46 task patterns. Evidence-grounded root cause:\n- The skill bridge only counts a task as skill-worthy if it **has a dossier** (`pattern_skill_bridge.go:41` — `JOIN dossiers`).\n- Dossiers are built only for patterns with `strength ≥ promotionThreshold = 0.65` (`pattern_dossier.go:67`, `pattern_candidates.go:27`).\n- **Max task strength here is 0.62 — below the gate.** So 0 of 46 task patterns get a dossier → 0 skill candidates. Only the top risk (0.678) and one procedure (0.65) cleared the bar.\n- Secondary: the task patterns that exist are git command n-grams (`commit:push — git push ▷ git status`), not intent-rich user tasks — so even lowering the threshold would surface low-value \"skills\" first. The genuine recurring-intent signal didn't cluster above 0.65.\n\n**Suggestions for Thomas** (his call): seed dossiers for the top-N tasks regardless of the global threshold, lower the task promotion bar specifically, or weight intent-backed tasks above command-sequence tasks so real tasks outrank git plumbing.\n\nI didn't touch his PR — just evaluated it. The corpus is now built locally (additive/rebuildable) if you want to poke at it: `/tmp/entire-brain-v44 patterns` (and `patterns skills`). I'm back on `claude/brain-dash-tui`.\n\nWant me to write this up as a PR #44 review comment, or keep it here for you to relay?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2086,"cache_read_input_tokens":561542,"output_tokens":969,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2086,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":561542,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2086},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cc99Kyeb7FKBUPxo7YgiB","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a84b050-d9af-4396-b68d-b0fbaf5e4d86","timestamp":"2026-06-17T16:26:13.416Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
