{"parentUuid":"21785c64-a428-4b27-a982-5c61c57f00c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01PoCHkpMsCYGSusR4q87bfy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YWbiB88M2HijzfFyLyZQMB","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/README.md","limit":70},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3315,"cache_read_input_tokens":597220,"output_tokens":1228,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":597220,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcAxHgPSRzQsVjfmcGRCD","type":"assistant","uuid":"536a73f8-692e-42cb-b0bc-34ae754f1e13","timestamp":"2026-06-18T15:22:42.562Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"536a73f8-692e-42cb-b0bc-34ae754f1e13","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d2a1b967-c286-46f3-b560-f6bab2912f4e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YWbiB88M2HijzfFyLyZQMB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Entire Brain\n2\t\n3\tEntire Brain is an external-command plugin for the Entire CLI. It builds a\n4\tlocal, inspectable \"brain\" for a repository from Entire session history, seeded\n5\trepository context, a local history index, an index of the brain's own docs (seed\n6\tsummaries and copied repo markdown), optional semantic records from `entire-sem`,\n7\tand a curated layer of durable facts distilled from past sessions.\n8\t\n9\tThe plugin binary is named `entire-brain` and is invoked through Entire as:\n10\t\n11\t```sh\n12\tentire brain\n13\t```\n14\t\n15\tGenerated brain artifacts are local and inspectable by default: deterministic\n16\trefresh/index/retrieval reads local repositories and writes local plugin data,\n17\tand the MCP adapter is stdio-only. Optional agent-gated steps can send selected\n18\tcontext to the configured agent (`refresh --agent auto`, `distill --agent\n19\tcodex|claude-code`, `recall --expand`, and judged evals). Use `--agent none`,\n20\t`--dry-run`, `--agent command` with a local command, or loopback-only Ollama to\n21\tavoid hosted model egress. Strict no-egress mode (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS=1` or\n22\t`ENTIRE_BRAIN_LOCAL_ONLY=1`) can only enforce no-agent, dry-run, and Ollama\n23\tpaths whose URLs, redirects, and resolved dial targets stay loopback-only;\n24\tarbitrary `--agent command` runners are trusted local commands but not\n25\tenforceably loopback-only. Separately, repos that configure a\n26\t`checkpoint_remote` allow `refresh` (and its `sessions` export stage) to `git fetch` checkpoint history\n27\tfrom that remote into a throwaway temp repo unless no-egress mode is set.\n28\t\n29\t## Install\n30\t\n31\t```sh\n32\tmise install\n33\tmise run check\n34\tmise run build\n35\tentire plugin install ./entire-brain\n36\tentire brain\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t## Common Workflows\n40\t\n41\t### Create Or Refresh A Brain\n42\t\n43\t```sh\n44\tentire brain refresh\n45\tentire brain refresh --agent none\n46\tentire brain refresh --output /tmp/repo-brain\n47\tentire brain refresh --force\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\t`refresh` is the normal entry point. It writes the newest known checkpoint\n51\tversion of every discoverable Entire session into the persistent brain\n52\tdirectory, builds deterministic repository seed context, runs `entire sem`, and\n53\tbuilds the local semantic context graph used by the `inspect`\n54\t`code`/`context`/`impact`/`changes`/`tests` commands and `brief`. It also derives\n55\tthe local decision/rationale history index from the exported sessions and a doc\n56\tindex over the brain's seed markdown. `--agent` controls optional seed synthesis:\n57\tthe default is `auto`, which uses Codex when available, then Claude Code when\n58\tavailable, otherwise deterministic seed-only mode. `--output` writes a complete\n59\tbrain to an explicit directory. `--force` rebuilds generated sources and\n60\toverwrites an explicit output directory when one is provided.\n61\t\n62\tThe semantic refresh stores semantic snapshots, a SQLite query store, metrics,\n63\tparse cache, and branch overlays in the local brain directory. It refuses dirty\n64\tworktrees unless semantic worktree indexing is explicitly enabled through the\n65\tadvanced `refresh index --worktree` maintenance path.\n66\t\n67\tUse `--worktree` on `refresh index` only when you intentionally want the current\n68\tdirty worktree represented. Bundle export rejects worktree-backed semantic indexes.\n69\t`repair` rebuilds derived semantic stores from the active local snapshot.\n70\t`reset --semantic-only --force` removes semantic artifacts and manifest metadata"}]},"uuid":"e5d14634-4bff-43d0-afd3-6e49b1bd14a9","timestamp":"2026-06-18T15:22:42.569Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/README.md","content":"# Entire Brain\n\nEntire Brain is an external-command plugin for the Entire CLI. It builds a\nlocal, inspectable \"brain\" for a repository from Entire session history, seeded\nrepository context, a local history index, an index of the brain's own docs (seed\nsummaries and copied repo markdown), optional semantic records from `entire-sem`,\nand a curated layer of durable facts distilled from past sessions.\n\nThe plugin binary is named `entire-brain` and is invoked through Entire as:\n\n```sh\nentire brain\n```\n\nGenerated brain artifacts are local and inspectable by default: deterministic\nrefresh/index/retrieval reads local repositories and writes local plugin data,\nand the MCP adapter is stdio-only. Optional agent-gated steps can send selected\ncontext to the configured agent (`refresh --agent auto`, `distill --agent\ncodex|claude-code`, `recall --expand`, and judged evals). Use `--agent none`,\n`--dry-run`, `--agent command` with a local command, or loopback-only Ollama to\navoid hosted model egress. Strict no-egress mode (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS=1` or\n`ENTIRE_BRAIN_LOCAL_ONLY=1`) can only enforce no-agent, dry-run, and Ollama\npaths whose URLs, redirects, and resolved dial targets stay loopback-only;\narbitrary `--agent command` runners are trusted local commands but not\nenforceably loopback-only. Separately, repos that configure a\n`checkpoint_remote` allow `refresh` (and its `sessions` export stage) to `git fetch` checkpoint history\nfrom that remote into a throwaway temp repo unless no-egress mode is set.\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\nmise install\nmise run check\nmise run build\nentire plugin install ./entire-brain\nentire brain\n```\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### Create Or Refresh A Brain\n\n```sh\nentire brain refresh\nentire brain refresh --agent none\nentire brain refresh --output /tmp/repo-brain\nentire brain refresh --force\n```\n\n`refresh` is the normal entry point. It writes the newest known checkpoint\nversion of every discoverable Entire session into the persistent brain\ndirectory, builds deterministic repository seed context, runs `entire sem`, and\nbuilds the local semantic context graph used by the `inspect`\n`code`/`context`/`impact`/`changes`/`tests` commands and `brief`. It also derives\nthe local decision/rationale history index from the exported sessions and a doc\nindex over the brain's seed markdown. `--agent` controls optional seed synthesis:\nthe default is `auto`, which uses Codex when available, then Claude Code when\navailable, otherwise deterministic seed-only mode. `--output` writes a complete\nbrain to an explicit directory. `--force` rebuilds generated sources and\noverwrites an explicit output directory when one is provided.\n\nThe semantic refresh stores semantic snapshots, a SQLite query store, metrics,\nparse cache, and branch overlays in the local brain directory. It refuses dirty\nworktrees unless semantic worktree indexing is explicitly enabled through the\nadvanced `refresh index --worktree` maintenance path.\n\nUse `--worktree` on `refresh index` only when you intentionally want the current\ndirty worktree represented. Bundle export rejects worktree-backed semantic indexes.\n`repair` rebuilds derived semantic stores from the active local snapshot.\n`reset --semantic-only --force` removes semantic artifacts and manifest metadata","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":395}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"536a73f8-692e-42cb-b0bc-34ae754f1e13","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"e5d14634-4bff-43d0-afd3-6e49b1bd14a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01PoCHkpMsCYGSusR4q87bfy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014Fa5sMtKqf1iUqFYuCpKx5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release-blockers.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3315,"cache_read_input_tokens":597220,"output_tokens":1228,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3315,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1228,"cache_read_input_tokens":597220,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3315},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcAxHgPSRzQsVjfmcGRCD","type":"assistant","uuid":"e5f77d1e-c6d1-456a-849b-f40ce9f467db","timestamp":"2026-06-18T15:22:42.789Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"e5f77d1e-c6d1-456a-849b-f40ce9f467db","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d2a1b967-c286-46f3-b560-f6bab2912f4e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Fa5sMtKqf1iUqFYuCpKx5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Release Blockers\n2\t\n3\tA register of release-gating findings from the PR #33 review (2026-06-11),\n4\tkept next to the audit so a release decision can see what is open, what was\n5\tfixed, and exactly why. The standard for this file is the eval ledger's:\n6\texplicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n7\t\n8\t## RESOLVED AS CLAIM DEMOTION — B1: Answer-bearing query hints invalidated the old replay-lab proof\n9\t\n10\t**The claim under audit.** `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` previously treated\n11\tthree replay-lab suites as citable proof that history/MCP/Radar context improved\n12\tagent outcomes without handing over hidden validation or expected text. That\n13\tattribution was unsupported.\n14\t\n15\t**The confound.** `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` injects `brain_queries` into\n16\tbrain/MCP-arm prompts only; the `no_brain` arm receives none. In the retained\n17\tpre-B1 suites, several `brain_queries` contained answer-bearing identifiers,\n18\thidden-test names, or near-verbatim hidden-validation strings. The old\n19\tcomparison therefore measured *(answer-bearing hint + brain)* versus *(no hint,\n20\tno brain)*, not brain value alone.\n21\t\n22\t**Fixes landed.**\n23\t\n24\t- `brain_query_leak_audit` now rejects answer-bearing `brain_queries` before a\n25\t  panel can run. It checks code-shaped identifiers and verbatim 3+-word phrases\n26\t  against hidden fix text and paths, expected files, hidden validation commands,\n27\t  expected-string greps, hidden test names, and validation fixture contents.\n28\t- All committed benchmark task queries that tripped the auditor were rewritten\n29\t  to symptom-level retrieval terms. The all-task sweep now reports zero flagged\n30\t  task files.\n31\t- The retained evidence manifest is stricter again: even in `no_release_claim`\n32\t  mode it requires zero hard integrity flags.\n33\t- The old confounded retained suites were removed from\n34\t  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release` and replaced with clean reruns.\n35\t\n36\t**Clean rerun result (2026-06-11).** Item 3 is now complete: the three promoted\n37\tsuites were rerun from a clean checkout with the sanitized task configs, four\n38\trepetitions per side, retained panel provenance, and host paths redacted before\n39\tcommit. The independent audit now reports 3 suites, 24 records, 24/24 provenance\n40\tcomplete, 0 hard integrity flags, 8 MCP-verified datapoints, 4 completed\n41\tnamed-tool Radar datapoints, and 0 proof-ready comparisons.\n42\t\n43\t| Clean retained suite | Outcome |\n44\t|---|---|\n45\t| `release-candidate-entire-brain-schema-contract-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but noisy: pass rate 50% -> 75%, mean score 86.5 -> 87.75, `proof_ready=false`. |\n46\t| `release-candidate-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.25 -> 91.25, `proof_ready=false`. |\n47\t| `release-candidate-cli-radar-mcp-del-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.5 -> 90.5, `proof_ready=false`. |\n48\t\n49\t**Current release implication.** B1 is resolved as an integrity/confound blocker:\n50\tthe retained release lane no longer contains answer-bearing query-hint artifacts.\n51\tIt is still `no_release_claim`, because the clean reruns did not produce a\n52\tproof-ready replay-lab lift. Any future agent-lift claim needs harder clean\n53\tretained tasks that survive the proof-ready gate; the old numbers stay removed\n54\tfrom the release story.\n55\t\n56\tOperationalization note: the literal \"any token\" wording from the review is not\n57\timplemented because it would false-flag ordinary symptom text. The enforced rule\n58\tis code-shaped identifiers plus verbatim 3+-word phrases, with the known residual\n59\tthat 1-2 word plain-English overlaps are not flagged.\n60\t\n61\t## RESOLVED — fixed during review on this branch\n62\t\n63\t**R1 — Eval label discipline orphaned the history-eval pipeline** (fixed in\n64\t`15e7aaa`). `validateEvalTask` rejected `history-eval-gen` output and every\n65\tretained task file; `eval-compare` hard-errored on its own default eval-gen\n66\toutput. Fix separates ground-*truth* (same explicit labels, same source →\n67\tcomparable) from evidence *grade* (human/judge-refined → claimable);\n68\thistory-eval now declares `provenance_silver`, legacy files default to it,\n69\tand side-dependent truths (`source_match`, runtime judge) stay gated behind\n70\t`--allow-proxy-comparison`. Covered by a new gen→load→run→compare seam test.\n71\t\n72\t**R2 — Retrieval panic on the loopback guard's own rejection path** (fixed in\n73\t`15e7aaa`). `configuredEmbedder` dereferenced the nil returned for a\n74\tnon-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBED_URL`; every `search`/`vsearch`/`query`\n75\tcrashed in the exact scenario the guard hardens. Now degrades to the bundled\n76\tModel2Vec embedder with a warning; regression test added.\n77\t\n78\t**R3 — Brain write-lock scoping** (fixed in `15e7aaa`). Export held the\n79\texclusive lock across the minutes-long transcript phase while every other\n80\tuser times out at 10s — failing a concurrent distill's FINAL flush (an\n81\thours-long run killed at its last step) — and `openHistoryFTS` took the write\n82\tlock on the query READ path, serializing all searches. Export now locks only\n83\tthe shared-artifact phases; FTS opens fresh indexes lock-free and\n84\tdouble-checks freshness under the lock only for rebuilds.\n85\t\n86\t**R4 — Silent full re-distill on upgrade** (fixed alongside this file). The\n87\tfingerprint salt plus the stable-branch-dir rename invalidated every existing\n88\tcache entry, and the shipped \"legacy key\" fallback could never match (a\n89\tlegacy-format fingerprint never equals a salted one) — the first post-upgrade\n90\trun would re-distill the entire corpus (observed scale: ~14h of agent calls\n91\tfor a 2,640-session brain). Fixed with lazy grandfathering: the legacy\n92\tformula is kept genuinely computable (including pre-rename transcript paths),\n93\ta matching legacy entry counts as cached and is rewritten under the new\n94\tkey/format on first touch, and the transcript path is no longer hashed into\n95\tthe new fingerprint at all — storage layout is not identity, and hashing it\n96\tre-invalidates the world on every future layout change. The filtered-session\n97\tcarry-through, which copied legacy-format fingerprints under new-format keys\n98\t(making them permanently unmatchable), now preserves entries under their own\n99\tkeys. Covered by `TestDistillCacheGrandfathersLegacyEntries`, including the\n100\trenamed-branch-dir case and the changed-content negative.\n101\t"}]},"uuid":"2c6246cd-ba62-4070-897a-3f48f4b94630","timestamp":"2026-06-18T15:22:42.800Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release-blockers.md","content":"# Release Blockers\n\nA register of release-gating findings from the PR #33 review (2026-06-11),\nkept next to the audit so a release decision can see what is open, what was\nfixed, and exactly why. The standard for this file is the eval ledger's:\nexplicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n\n## RESOLVED AS CLAIM DEMOTION — B1: Answer-bearing query hints invalidated the old replay-lab proof\n\n**The claim under audit.** `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` previously treated\nthree replay-lab suites as citable proof that history/MCP/Radar context improved\nagent outcomes without handing over hidden validation or expected text. That\nattribution was unsupported.\n\n**The confound.** `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` injects `brain_queries` into\nbrain/MCP-arm prompts only; the `no_brain` arm receives none. In the retained\npre-B1 suites, several `brain_queries` contained answer-bearing identifiers,\nhidden-test names, or near-verbatim hidden-validation strings. The old\ncomparison therefore measured *(answer-bearing hint + brain)* versus *(no hint,\nno brain)*, not brain value alone.\n\n**Fixes landed.**\n\n- `brain_query_leak_audit` now rejects answer-bearing `brain_queries` before a\n  panel can run. It checks code-shaped identifiers and verbatim 3+-word phrases\n  against hidden fix text and paths, expected files, hidden validation commands,\n  expected-string greps, hidden test names, and validation fixture contents.\n- All committed benchmark task queries that tripped the auditor were rewritten\n  to symptom-level retrieval terms. The all-task sweep now reports zero flagged\n  task files.\n- The retained evidence manifest is stricter again: even in `no_release_claim`\n  mode it requires zero hard integrity flags.\n- The old confounded retained suites were removed from\n  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release` and replaced with clean reruns.\n\n**Clean rerun result (2026-06-11).** Item 3 is now complete: the three promoted\nsuites were rerun from a clean checkout with the sanitized task configs, four\nrepetitions per side, retained panel provenance, and host paths redacted before\ncommit. The independent audit now reports 3 suites, 24 records, 24/24 provenance\ncomplete, 0 hard integrity flags, 8 MCP-verified datapoints, 4 completed\nnamed-tool Radar datapoints, and 0 proof-ready comparisons.\n\n| Clean retained suite | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `release-candidate-entire-brain-schema-contract-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but noisy: pass rate 50% -> 75%, mean score 86.5 -> 87.75, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.25 -> 91.25, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-cli-radar-mcp-del-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.5 -> 90.5, `proof_ready=false`. |\n\n**Current release implication.** B1 is resolved as an integrity/confound blocker:\nthe retained release lane no longer contains answer-bearing query-hint artifacts.\nIt is still `no_release_claim`, because the clean reruns did not produce a\nproof-ready replay-lab lift. Any future agent-lift claim needs harder clean\nretained tasks that survive the proof-ready gate; the old numbers stay removed\nfrom the release story.\n\nOperationalization note: the literal \"any token\" wording from the review is not\nimplemented because it would false-flag ordinary symptom text. The enforced rule\nis code-shaped identifiers plus verbatim 3+-word phrases, with the known residual\nthat 1-2 word plain-English overlaps are not flagged.\n\n## RESOLVED — fixed during review on this branch\n\n**R1 — Eval label discipline orphaned the history-eval pipeline** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `validateEvalTask` rejected `history-eval-gen` output and every\nretained task file; `eval-compare` hard-errored on its own default eval-gen\noutput. Fix separates ground-*truth* (same explicit labels, same source →\ncomparable) from evidence *grade* (human/judge-refined → claimable);\nhistory-eval now declares `provenance_silver`, legacy files default to it,\nand side-dependent truths (`source_match`, runtime judge) stay gated behind\n`--allow-proxy-comparison`. Covered by a new gen→load→run→compare seam test.\n\n**R2 — Retrieval panic on the loopback guard's own rejection path** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `configuredEmbedder` dereferenced the nil returned for a\nnon-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBED_URL`; every `search`/`vsearch`/`query`\ncrashed in the exact scenario the guard hardens. Now degrades to the bundled\nModel2Vec embedder with a warning; regression test added.\n\n**R3 — Brain write-lock scoping** (fixed in `15e7aaa`). Export held the\nexclusive lock across the minutes-long transcript phase while every other\nuser times out at 10s — failing a concurrent distill's FINAL flush (an\nhours-long run killed at its last step) — and `openHistoryFTS` took the write\nlock on the query READ path, serializing all searches. Export now locks only\nthe shared-artifact phases; FTS opens fresh indexes lock-free and\ndouble-checks freshness under the lock only for rebuilds.\n\n**R4 — Silent full re-distill on upgrade** (fixed alongside this file). The\nfingerprint salt plus the stable-branch-dir rename invalidated every existing\ncache entry, and the shipped \"legacy key\" fallback could never match (a\nlegacy-format fingerprint never equals a salted one) — the first post-upgrade\nrun would re-distill the entire corpus (observed scale: ~14h of agent calls\nfor a 2,640-session brain). Fixed with lazy grandfathering: the legacy\nformula is kept genuinely computable (including pre-rename transcript paths),\na matching legacy entry counts as cached and is rewritten under the new\nkey/format on first touch, and the transcript path is no longer hashed into\nthe new fingerprint at all — storage layout is not identity, and hashing it\nre-invalidates the world on every future layout change. The filtered-session\ncarry-through, which copied legacy-format fingerprints under new-format keys\n(making them permanently unmatchable), now preserves entries under their own\nkeys. Covered by `TestDistillCacheGrandfathersLegacyEntries`, including the\nrenamed-branch-dir case and the changed-content negative.\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e5f77d1e-c6d1-456a-849b-f40ce9f467db","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
