{"parentUuid":"47ce0211-79ee-4a57-abc9-fdda33c584fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011kd1uM8ZettgtHTtdAVSws","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the formal readiness audit (the current verdict + open items):"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2574,"cache_read_input_tokens":605722,"output_tokens":962,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2574,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":605722,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2574},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcAxKiDswtej2Z7xNJEQC","type":"assistant","uuid":"f66e595d-ea53-46bd-95d9-def4fc726aa5","timestamp":"2026-06-18T15:23:07.959Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"f66e595d-ea53-46bd-95d9-def4fc726aa5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011kd1uM8ZettgtHTtdAVSws","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018W6HR2twQU3UGGv1Dxcvu7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md","limit":130},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2574,"cache_read_input_tokens":605722,"output_tokens":962,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2574,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":605722,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2574},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcAxKiDswtej2Z7xNJEQC","type":"assistant","uuid":"ecbaadda-b05e-4040-a508-eca62afc309e","timestamp":"2026-06-18T15:23:08.971Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"ecbaadda-b05e-4040-a508-eca62afc309e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d2a1b967-c286-46f3-b560-f6bab2912f4e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018W6HR2twQU3UGGv1Dxcvu7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Release Readiness Audit\n2\t\n3\tThis audit tracks the loose ends that need to close before `entire-brain`,\n4\t`entire-sem`, and `entire-replay-lab` can ship with honest claims.\n5\t\n6\t## Distill Performance\n7\t\n8\tLarge repos can make `entire brain distill` run for many hours because each\n9\ttranscript chunk may become one extraction agent call and each candidate set can\n10\talso require reconcile work. Without a local preflight, users cannot tell whether\n11\ta run means tens, hundreds, or thousands of calls.\n12\t\n13\tImplemented claim-control surfaces:\n14\t\n15\t- `entire brain distill --dry-run --json` reports sessions, cached sessions,\n16\t  preprocessed bytes, scheduled chunks, `chunks_if_uncached`, branch spread,\n17\t  largest sessions, `schema_version`, and an upper bound on extraction plus\n18\t  reconcile agent calls without calling an agent or writing facts. Cached-session\n19\t  rows keep `chunks` as scheduled work and use `chunks_if_uncached` for the warm\n20\t  cache capacity estimate.\n21\t- Distill summaries now include additive cache/timing fields:\n22\t  `cache_hits`, `failed_chunks`, `preprocessed_bytes`, `extraction_seconds`,\n23\t  `reconcile_seconds`, `write_seconds`, and `total_seconds`, plus the\n24\t  self-describing run config and actual call counts needed for timed-run\n25\t  evidence: `agent`, `model`, `effort`, `jobs`, `effective_extraction_jobs`,\n26\t  `max_chunk_bytes`, `confidence_threshold`, `extraction_agent_calls`,\n27\t  `reconcile_agent_calls`, and `total_agent_calls`.\n28\t- `--jobs N` parallelizes extraction calls only. Candidate reconciliation and\n29\t  all writes still happen in deterministic session/chunk order.\n30\t- `--agent ollama --model <model>` can use local loopback Ollama through\n31\t  `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate`; the HTTP\n32\t  transport bypasses proxies and resolves/dials only loopback IP targets.\n33\t- The retained distill evidence now includes a non-cached fake-Ollama\n34\t  `go test -json` artifact for the local-model contract: the distill command sends\n35\t  the selected model to loopback `/api/generate`, requests non-streaming output,\n36\t  avoids the `ollama` PATH binary, ignores proxy/custom TLS hooks, and rejects\n37\t  non-loopback URLs or redirects without requiring a real external model.\n38\t- `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py` audits retained performance\n39\t  artifacts for release proof: one dry-run JSON, one timed `--jobs 1` summary,\n40\t  and one timed `--jobs N` summary. It requires matching agent/model/branch/force\n41\t  / max-chunk-bytes / confidence config, retained artifact hashes, retained command-token\n42\t  provenance with an explicit non-`auto` agent, target provenance\n43\t  (`repo`, `repo_key`, `source_head`, `brain_manifest_sha256`, and\n44\t  `claim_scope`), no missing transcripts, branch totals that add up, matching\n45\t  cache-hit counts, no warnings or failed chunks, bounded reconcile calls,\n46\t  timing components that fit under `total_seconds`, comparable chunk/call/output\n47\t  summaries, effective parallelism greater than 1, and observed `total_seconds`\n48\t  speedup above the manifest's `min_speedup`. It also requires the retained\n49\t  fake-Ollama contract artifact and all required loopback/no-egress tests to pass.\n50\t- `mise run distill:evidence` checks committed distill artifacts without\n51\t  rewriting them, while `distill:evidence:update` regenerates the audit report\n52\t  only after the validator passes. The current retained artifacts are scoped to\n53\t  this repository and a deterministic local command agent: they prove the\n54\t  extraction scheduler/evidence gate, not hosted-model quality or the\n55\t  frontend/entire.io 24h claim.\n56\t\n57\tClaim policy: do not claim distill is \"fast\" until a real large-repo dry-run and\n58\ttimed run show the call count and wall-time improvement.\n59\t\n60\tRetained local scheduler evidence collected on this repo: the committed\n61\t`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json` targets\n62\t`github.com/ashtom/entire-brain` at the retained measured head, uses a\n63\tdeterministic local command agent, and passes `mise run distill:evidence`.\n64\tThe retained dry-run reported 147 sessions, 7,419,024 preprocessed bytes, 159\n65\tscheduled extraction chunks, and 159 extraction calls. The paired timed summaries\n66\tshowed `--jobs 1` and `--jobs 4` produced matching summaries with zero failed\n67\tchunks, and the observed wall-time speedup was about 2x. This validates the\n68\tparallel extraction scheduler and retained evidence gate, but it is not target\n69\tfrontend performance proof. The same manifest also retains the fake loopback\n70\tOllama contract test artifact, which supports local-model/Ollama wiring and\n71\tno-egress safety claims without supporting real-model fact quality.\n72\t\n73\tBlocked evidence collection: the target large session repo and retained timed\n74\trun artifacts are still needed before any public frontend/large-repo performance\n75\tclaim.\n76\t\n77\t## Facts Vs Raw Sessions\n78\t\n79\tFacts retrieval must be compared against history, unified-query, and preprocessed\n80\tsession baselines before release claims say it is better.\n81\t\n82\tImplemented eval surfaces:\n83\t\n84\t- `entire brain facts eval --retriever facts|history|query|raw-sessions` compares\n85\t  facts, history, unified query, and preprocessed session chunk arms over the\n86\t  same task file.\n87\t- Eval task JSON now accepts `source_session_id`, `source_transcript_path`, and\n88\t  `source_lines` so preprocessed session baselines can cite retained source\n89\t  anchors; generated task files populate those fields, and line anchors are\n90\t  source-overlap proxies rather than proof labels.\n91\t- The eval `query` arm is read-only and lexical inside the harness, so it does\n92\t  not write embedding caches or call an embedder while measuring baselines.\n93\t- History and unified-query eval arms filter session-derived history by the\n94\t  task branch, matching the branch scope already used by facts and raw-session\n95\t  retrievers.\n96\t- Eval summaries include `retriever`, `latency_ms`, and `relevance_source`\n97\t  (`explicit_label`, `partial_explicit_label`, `mixed_explicit_source_match`,\n98\t  `source_match`, `judge`, or `none`), so charts can separate source-match proxy\n99\t  credit from labeled recall and spot query arms that mix fact labels with other\n100\t  source types. The human table now prints each row's relevance/label source and\n101\t  warns when non-proof relevance rows are present.\n102\t- `eval-compare` includes a per-metric winner and explicit claim text, and now\n103\t  rejects non-proof or different relevance sources unless\n104\t  `--allow-proxy-comparison` is explicit. Same-source `source_match` proxy is\n105\t  still proxy evidence, not proof evidence. Its JSON metrics also include\n106\t  `evidence_basis` (`proof_labels`, `proxy_or_mixed`, `operational`, or\n107\t  `unavailable`) and `release_claimable`, so an allowed proxy comparison cannot\n108\t  silently become proof copy.\n109\t- `facts eval` validates `label_source`; task files with `relevant` ids must\n110\t  say whether labels are `human`, `judge_refined`, or `provenance_silver`.\n111\t- `eval-compare` also rejects differing non-empty `run_config.tasks_sha256` and\n112\t  `run_config.brain_manifest_sha256` values unless the matching override is\n113\t  explicit, so same-id eval runs with different task labels or brain state\n114\t  cannot masquerade as paired proof.\n115\t- `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py` audits retained facts-eval\n116\t  artifacts for release proof: proof manifests require the four retriever\n117\t  summaries, matching non-empty task and brain-manifest hashes, no proxy/missing\n118\t  /mismatch overrides, empty missing-task sets, and required comparison metrics\n119\t  that are significant, `release_claimable: true`, and\n120\t  `evidence_basis: \"proof_labels\"`. The audit also requires top-level\n121\t  `release_pairing_ready: true`, a positive paired row count, and at least one\n122\t  required proof-label claim where the `facts` arm beats `raw-sessions`, so a\n123\t  proxy or unrelated comparison cannot be promoted into a facts-vs-raw claim by\n124\t  editing manifest text. It also supports an explicit\n125\t  `claim_policy: \"no_release_claim\"` manifest backed by `facts status --json`;\n126\t  that passes only when the facts arm is not ready, has zero active facts, and\n127\t  carries retained freshness provenance (`generated_at`, `repo_head`, and\n128\t  `brain_manifest_sha256`).\n129\t- The retained proof-mode contract fixture under\n130\t  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture` exercises a"}]},"uuid":"c00c97a8-5f4a-41ec-b061-0753bc9eb5d8","timestamp":"2026-06-18T15:23:08.989Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_readiness_audit.md","content":"# Release Readiness Audit\n\nThis audit tracks the loose ends that need to close before `entire-brain`,\n`entire-sem`, and `entire-replay-lab` can ship with honest claims.\n\n## Distill Performance\n\nLarge repos can make `entire brain distill` run for many hours because each\ntranscript chunk may become one extraction agent call and each candidate set can\nalso require reconcile work. Without a local preflight, users cannot tell whether\na run means tens, hundreds, or thousands of calls.\n\nImplemented claim-control surfaces:\n\n- `entire brain distill --dry-run --json` reports sessions, cached sessions,\n  preprocessed bytes, scheduled chunks, `chunks_if_uncached`, branch spread,\n  largest sessions, `schema_version`, and an upper bound on extraction plus\n  reconcile agent calls without calling an agent or writing facts. Cached-session\n  rows keep `chunks` as scheduled work and use `chunks_if_uncached` for the warm\n  cache capacity estimate.\n- Distill summaries now include additive cache/timing fields:\n  `cache_hits`, `failed_chunks`, `preprocessed_bytes`, `extraction_seconds`,\n  `reconcile_seconds`, `write_seconds`, and `total_seconds`, plus the\n  self-describing run config and actual call counts needed for timed-run\n  evidence: `agent`, `model`, `effort`, `jobs`, `effective_extraction_jobs`,\n  `max_chunk_bytes`, `confidence_threshold`, `extraction_agent_calls`,\n  `reconcile_agent_calls`, and `total_agent_calls`.\n- `--jobs N` parallelizes extraction calls only. Candidate reconciliation and\n  all writes still happen in deterministic session/chunk order.\n- `--agent ollama --model <model>` can use local loopback Ollama through\n  `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate`; the HTTP\n  transport bypasses proxies and resolves/dials only loopback IP targets.\n- The retained distill evidence now includes a non-cached fake-Ollama\n  `go test -json` artifact for the local-model contract: the distill command sends\n  the selected model to loopback `/api/generate`, requests non-streaming output,\n  avoids the `ollama` PATH binary, ignores proxy/custom TLS hooks, and rejects\n  non-loopback URLs or redirects without requiring a real external model.\n- `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py` audits retained performance\n  artifacts for release proof: one dry-run JSON, one timed `--jobs 1` summary,\n  and one timed `--jobs N` summary. It requires matching agent/model/branch/force\n  / max-chunk-bytes / confidence config, retained artifact hashes, retained command-token\n  provenance with an explicit non-`auto` agent, target provenance\n  (`repo`, `repo_key`, `source_head`, `brain_manifest_sha256`, and\n  `claim_scope`), no missing transcripts, branch totals that add up, matching\n  cache-hit counts, no warnings or failed chunks, bounded reconcile calls,\n  timing components that fit under `total_seconds`, comparable chunk/call/output\n  summaries, effective parallelism greater than 1, and observed `total_seconds`\n  speedup above the manifest's `min_speedup`. It also requires the retained\n  fake-Ollama contract artifact and all required loopback/no-egress tests to pass.\n- `mise run distill:evidence` checks committed distill artifacts without\n  rewriting them, while `distill:evidence:update` regenerates the audit report\n  only after the validator passes. The current retained artifacts are scoped to\n  this repository and a deterministic local command agent: they prove the\n  extraction scheduler/evidence gate, not hosted-model quality or the\n  frontend/entire.io 24h claim.\n\nClaim policy: do not claim distill is \"fast\" until a real large-repo dry-run and\ntimed run show the call count and wall-time improvement.\n\nRetained local scheduler evidence collected on this repo: the committed\n`benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json` targets\n`github.com/ashtom/entire-brain` at the retained measured head, uses a\ndeterministic local command agent, and passes `mise run distill:evidence`.\nThe retained dry-run reported 147 sessions, 7,419,024 preprocessed bytes, 159\nscheduled extraction chunks, and 159 extraction calls. The paired timed summaries\nshowed `--jobs 1` and `--jobs 4` produced matching summaries with zero failed\nchunks, and the observed wall-time speedup was about 2x. This validates the\nparallel extraction scheduler and retained evidence gate, but it is not target\nfrontend performance proof. The same manifest also retains the fake loopback\nOllama contract test artifact, which supports local-model/Ollama wiring and\nno-egress safety claims without supporting real-model fact quality.\n\nBlocked evidence collection: the target large session repo and retained timed\nrun artifacts are still needed before any public frontend/large-repo performance\nclaim.\n\n## Facts Vs Raw Sessions\n\nFacts retrieval must be compared against history, unified-query, and preprocessed\nsession baselines before release claims say it is better.\n\nImplemented eval surfaces:\n\n- `entire brain facts eval --retriever facts|history|query|raw-sessions` compares\n  facts, history, unified query, and preprocessed session chunk arms over the\n  same task file.\n- Eval task JSON now accepts `source_session_id`, `source_transcript_path`, and\n  `source_lines` so preprocessed session baselines can cite retained source\n  anchors; generated task files populate those fields, and line anchors are\n  source-overlap proxies rather than proof labels.\n- The eval `query` arm is read-only and lexical inside the harness, so it does\n  not write embedding caches or call an embedder while measuring baselines.\n- History and unified-query eval arms filter session-derived history by the\n  task branch, matching the branch scope already used by facts and raw-session\n  retrievers.\n- Eval summaries include `retriever`, `latency_ms`, and `relevance_source`\n  (`explicit_label`, `partial_explicit_label`, `mixed_explicit_source_match`,\n  `source_match`, `judge`, or `none`), so charts can separate source-match proxy\n  credit from labeled recall and spot query arms that mix fact labels with other\n  source types. The human table now prints each row's relevance/label source and\n  warns when non-proof relevance rows are present.\n- `eval-compare` includes a per-metric winner and explicit claim text, and now\n  rejects non-proof or different relevance sources unless\n  `--allow-proxy-comparison` is explicit. Same-source `source_match` proxy is\n  still proxy evidence, not proof evidence. Its JSON metrics also include\n  `evidence_basis` (`proof_labels`, `proxy_or_mixed`, `operational`, or\n  `unavailable`) and `release_claimable`, so an allowed proxy comparison cannot\n  silently become proof copy.\n- `facts eval` validates `label_source`; task files with `relevant` ids must\n  say whether labels are `human`, `judge_refined`, or `provenance_silver`.\n- `eval-compare` also rejects differing non-empty `run_config.tasks_sha256` and\n  `run_config.brain_manifest_sha256` values unless the matching override is\n  explicit, so same-id eval runs with different task labels or brain state\n  cannot masquerade as paired proof.\n- `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_facts_eval.py` audits retained facts-eval\n  artifacts for release proof: proof manifests require the four retriever\n  summaries, matching non-empty task and brain-manifest hashes, no proxy/missing\n  /mismatch overrides, empty missing-task sets, and required comparison metrics\n  that are significant, `release_claimable: true`, and\n  `evidence_basis: \"proof_labels\"`. The audit also requires top-level\n  `release_pairing_ready: true`, a positive paired row count, and at least one\n  required proof-label claim where the `facts` arm beats `raw-sessions`, so a\n  proxy or unrelated comparison cannot be promoted into a facts-vs-raw claim by\n  editing manifest text. It also supports an explicit\n  `claim_policy: \"no_release_claim\"` manifest backed by `facts status --json`;\n  that passes only when the facts arm is not ready, has zero active facts, and\n  carries retained freshness provenance (`generated_at`, `repo_head`, and\n  `brain_manifest_sha256`).\n- The retained proof-mode contract fixture under\n  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture` exercises a","numLines":130,"startLine":1,"totalLines":750}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ecbaadda-b05e-4040-a508-eca62afc309e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/brain-dash-tui","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
