{"parentUuid":"d2b6b2e9-865f-47ef-b2e3-737094aadd54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Lav1Q6vsyNia8frcmUhRCG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":87468,"output_tokens":5522,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":5522,"cache_read_input_tokens":87468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcB6YQdkKBaJr2m3J8NC7","type":"assistant","uuid":"e84e94b1-f453-4c69-9624-996a4e66ea55","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:11:12.186Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"e84e94b1-f453-4c69-9624-996a4e66ea55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Lav1Q6vsyNia8frcmUhRCG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fresh branch ready. Now the critical recon: I need an exact map of the proof infrastructure before authoring anything — the proof gate's precise criteria, what \"clean\" means operationally, why the current score is 0/3, and what's actually runnable locally vs. gated on model access. The harness files are huge (run.py 224KB, run_test.py 271KB), so I'll fan out parallel readers rather than pull them into context.\n\nGiven ultracode is on, I'll orchestrate this as a mapping workflow."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":87468,"output_tokens":5522,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":5522,"cache_read_input_tokens":87468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcB6YQdkKBaJr2m3J8NC7","type":"assistant","uuid":"3503a9f6-aea2-468e-bd7b-26c104a84fdd","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:11:14.624Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"3503a9f6-aea2-468e-bd7b-26c104a84fdd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Lav1Q6vsyNia8frcmUhRCG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018mGbKWm49k5zLvHMyZBpsY","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'proof-gap-recon',\n  description: 'Map the entire-brain proof infrastructure: proof gate, task schema/cleanliness, agent-lift harness runnability, why 0/3, distill perf, eval-ledger gates',\n  phases: [{ title: 'Map', detail: 'six parallel readers, one subsystem each' }],\n}\n\nphase('Map')\n\nconst ROOT = '/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain'\n\nconst common = `You are mapping a subsystem of the entire-brain repo at ${ROOT} (a Go CLI plugin + a Python benchmark/proof harness under benchmarks/agent-brain/). This is READ-ONLY reconnaissance — do NOT edit anything. Be surgical: do not dump whole files into your answer. Instead return a precise, citeable map with file:line references and SHORT quoted snippets (3-8 lines) of the key code. Where you are uncertain, say so explicitly. The repo enforces strict evidence discipline (no fabricated numbers, \"eval ledger\" standard). Your final text IS the deliverable — return a tight markdown report.`\n\nconst tasks = [\n  {\n    label: 'gate',\n    prompt: `${common}\n\nSUBSYSTEM: THE PROOF GATE (what makes a benchmark result \"proof_ready\").\nFind and explain EXACTLY how proof_ready (a.k.a proofReady / ProofReady) is computed. Search run.py, run_test.py, make_report.py, full_report.py, audit_release_matrix.py under benchmarks/agent-brain/.\nReport precisely:\n1. The exact predicate/criteria that set proof_ready true vs false (every condition, with thresholds and the file:line + quoted code).\n2. What \"noisy\", \"saturated\", \"negative\", \"no_release_claim\" mean operationally in this gate — the exact numeric/statistical definitions (e.g. variance thresholds, min effect size, significance test, min N, tie/saturation rules).\n3. Which statistic is the agent-lift measure (pass-rate delta? token delta? quality score delta?) and how its confidence/significance is decided.\n4. Any \"retained tasks\" / \"retain\"/\"clean\" concept the gate references.\nOutput a structured markdown map. Cite file:line for every claim.`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'task-schema',\n    prompt: `${common}\n\nSUBSYSTEM: TASK SCHEMA + WHAT \"CLEAN\" MEANS.\nThe benchmark tasks live in benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/*.json (54 of them). \nReport precisely:\n1. The full task JSON schema — every field and its meaning. Read 3-4 representative task files in full and the loader/validator code in run.py / run_test.py that parses tasks. Quote the schema-defining struct/dict.\n2. What makes a task \"clean\" vs \"leaky\"/\"confounded\" — especially the \"query-hint confound\" (the B1 confound described in docs/release-blockers.md). What field(s) can leak the answer into the prompt? How does the harness detect/forbid answer hints? Quote the exact check.\n3. What distinguishes an \"easy\"/\"saturated\" task from a \"hard\" task that produces signal. Any difficulty metadata.\n4. How a task declares the with-brain vs without-brain expectation, success criteria, and grader.\nRead docs/release-blockers.md (the B1 query-hint section) and benchmarks/agent-brain/README.md for the cleanliness rules. Cite file:line throughout.`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'harness-run',\n    prompt: `${common}\n\nSUBSYSTEM: AGENT-LIFT HARNESS — HOW RUNS EXECUTE + WHAT'S RUNNABLE LOCALLY.\nGoal: determine whether the with-brain vs without-brain agent-lift benchmark can be RUN in a local environment WITHOUT hosted-model API credentials, or what exactly it requires.\nReport precisely:\n1. The harness entry points: how run.py / run_test.py are invoked (CLI args, the run_cli_matrix.sh / run_cli_parallel.sh / run_opus_matrix.sh scripts). Quote the argparse / main.\n2. How an agent is actually driven per task: does it shell out to 'claude'/'codex'/'entire' CLIs? call an HTTP API? Is there a \"local command agent\" / mock / deterministic agent mode (grep for 'local', 'command agent', 'mock', 'fake', 'offline', 'dry')? Quote the agent-invocation code.\n3. EXACTLY what external access a real agent-lift run needs (which CLI binaries, which API keys/env vars, network). Be concrete.\n4. How with-brain vs without-brain conditions are set up (env vars, brain dir injection, MCP).\n5. Roughly how long / how many model calls a full clean suite is.\nCite file:line. Be explicit about what is deterministic/offline vs what needs model access.`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'why-0of3',\n    prompt: `${common}\n\nSUBSYSTEM: WHY THE CURRENT CLEAN SUITES SCORE 0/3 PROOF-READY.\nInvestigate the existing evidence to enumerate the clean suites and the EXACT reason each is not proof_ready.\nRead under benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/: release/ (summary.json files + README + manifest.json), semantic-clean-proof/ (report.json files + README), history-delivery-fix/ (report.json + README). Also read the verdicts in docs/release_readiness_audit.md and docs/release-blockers.md.\nReport precisely:\n1. Enumerate each \"clean\" suite/run that was attempted as an agent-lift proof, with its evidence path.\n2. For EACH, the measured numbers (pass-rate with vs without brain, N, deltas) and the EXACT gate reason it failed proof-ready: \"noisy\" (high variance / overlapping CI), \"saturated\" (both conditions near 100%, no headroom), \"negative\" (brain hurt or no effect), or \"confounded\" (query-hint). Quote the relevant summary.json/report.json fields and the readiness-audit verdict text.\n3. Synthesize: what PROPERTY must new tasks have to flip a suite to proof_ready (e.g. lower baseline pass-rate to escape saturation, tighter variance, clean prompts). Be concrete and grounded in the failure reasons.\nCite file:line / file paths for every number.`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'distill-perf',\n    prompt: `${common}\n\nSUBSYSTEM: DISTILL PERFORMANCE PROOF (P0.2).\nGoal: understand how to produce paired distill-timing evidence (distill --dry-run + timed --jobs 1 vs --jobs N on a large repo with a hosted model) and what the gate for calling distill \"fast\" requires.\nReport precisely:\n1. Read benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py: what evidence/manifest shape it expects, what it validates, what makes distill-perf evidence pass/fail its audit. Quote the key checks.\n2. Read the existing evidence/distill-perf/ files (manifest.json, jobs-1.json, jobs-4.json, dry-run.json, distill-perf-audit-report.*, README): what was measured, on what repo/model, and what the README says about provenance/limitations.\n3. In the Go CLI (internal/cli), find the 'distill' command: the --dry-run flag and the --jobs flag implementation. Is --dry-run deterministic/offline (no model)? Does the timed run require an agent/hosted model? Quote the relevant code (newDistillCommand / runDistill).\n4. What docs/release_press_release.md says must be proven before calling distill \"fast\". Quote it.\nCite file:line. Be explicit: which parts are runnable offline vs need a hosted model + a large target repo.`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'ledger-gates',\n    prompt: `${common}\n\nSUBSYSTEM: EVAL-LEDGER STANDARD + RELEASE MATRIX/CI GATES.\nReport precisely:\n1. Read docs/eval_ledger.md (if present) / any eval-ledger doc: the exact rules for what counts as a valid claim, required evidence fields, the \"no euphemism / explicit claims / exact evidence\" standard. Quote the rules.\n2. Read benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py: what it checks, what \"no_release_claim\" mode is, how it decides the overall release verdict. Quote key logic.\n3. Find the CI / mise wiring (search for 'mise', '*:evidence', release-evidence job in .github/workflows/, mise.toml, Makefile): which auditors run in CI and what gates them (which command refuses non-proof-ready evidence from becoming a claim). Quote the job/task definitions.\n4. How a new proof, once produced, gets registered as evidence and flips a claim from forbidden to allowed (the manifest/registration flow).\nCite file:line throughout.`,\n  },\n]\n\nconst maps = await parallel(tasks.map(t => () => agent(t.prompt, { label: t.label, phase: 'Map' })))\n\nreturn tasks.map((t, i) => ({ subsystem: t.label, map: maps[i] }))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":87468,"output_tokens":5522,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":5522,"cache_read_input_tokens":87468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcB6YQdkKBaJr2m3J8NC7","type":"assistant","uuid":"5167ebfd-e7c2-418f-928e-c0db75cb46fa","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:11:56.367Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
