{"parentUuid":"a376555e-a450-476e-bcab-b6676878cc39","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Mu8oV8JcdDZtNLdqQsNzNf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016dhdB6wrGubyWgnSuTUVqw","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/w5fk2l6k1.output","offset":21,"limit":11},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27467,"cache_read_input_tokens":107982,"output_tokens":5766,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27467,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5766,"cache_read_input_tokens":107982,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27467},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcB6su1LaU1EYqRMdWR6t","type":"assistant","uuid":"40e07231-c205-4a20-8d05-caecb94fd1e9","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:16:23.721Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"40e07231-c205-4a20-8d05-caecb94fd1e9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"730c809c-0f0c-4fd9-82a6-805198299ca1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016dhdB6wrGubyWgnSuTUVqw","type":"tool_result","content":"21\t    },\n22\t    {\n23\t      \"subsystem\": \"distill-perf\",\n24\t      \"map\": \"I now have a complete picture. Here is the deliverable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# DISTILL PERFORMANCE PROOF (P0.2) — Subsystem Map\\n\\nNote on git state: the prompt's git status lists these files as `D` (deleted), but they are **present on disk** in the working tree (`benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py`, all `evidence/distill-perf/*`, all `internal/cli/distill*.go`). The status snapshot is stale; everything below was read from the live files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. The auditor: `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py`\\n\\n**Evidence shape it expects** — a `manifest.json` (`schema == 1`) pointing at three sibling JSON artifacts plus a retained go-test artifact. Top-level validation (`validate_manifest`, lines 113-129) requires: `target` object, the three relative-path fields `dry_run`/`serial_run`/`parallel_run`, an `artifact_sha256` map, and a `commands` map.\\n\\n**What makes evidence PASS/FAIL** — `status` is `\\\"fail\\\"` if any flag is appended, else `\\\"pass\\\"`; `release_evidence` is `not flags` (audit_distill_perf.py:466-467). Key gates:\\n\\n- **Speedup gate (the \\\"fast\\\" bar)** — `min_speedup` must be `> 1.0` (raises if not, line 452-454). Observed speedup = `serial.total_seconds / parallel.total_seconds`; flagged if below threshold (lines 455-459):\\n  ```python\\n  speedup = float(serial[\\\"total_seconds\\\"]) / float(parallel[\\\"total_seconds\\\"])\\n  if speedup < float(min_speedup):\\n      flags.append(f\\\"speedup {speedup:.3f} < required {float(min_speedup):.3f}\\\")\\n  ```\\n- **Artifact + source integrity** — every JSON artifact's SHA-256 must match `artifact_sha256.*` (lines 303-311); every file in `DISTILL_PERF_SOURCE_PATHS` (the 4 `distill*.go` files + this auditor + `local-command-agent.py`, lines 22-26) must match `source_sha256` and exist under repo root (lines 314-335).\\n- **Dry-run shape** — `schema_version == 1`; a list of positive-number fields (`sessions`, `chunks`, `extraction_agent_calls`, …) at line 375; `missing_transcripts == 0`; empty `warnings`; `chunks == extraction_agent_calls`; `estimated_agent_calls_upper_bound == extraction + reconcile upper bound`; non-empty `branches` and `largest_sessions`; branch field sums must equal totals (`validate_branch_sums`, lines 338-345).\\n- **Command provenance** — `validate_command` (lines 273-300) requires each retained `commands.*` token list to contain `distill` and `--json`, the dry-run list to contain `--dry-run`, an **explicit `--agent` (not `\\\"\\\"`/`auto`)**, and `--model`/`--effort`/`--branch`/`--jobs`/`--max-chunk-bytes`/`--confidence` to **match the artifact's recorded fields**.\\n- **Serial vs parallel equivalence** — same agent/model/branch/force/chunk/confidence config (`config_tuple`, lines 236-245, checked at 401-404); `serial.jobs == 1`, `serial.extraction_jobs_cap ∈ {0,1}`; `parallel.jobs > 1` and `extraction_jobs_cap > 1` (lines 436-443); the output summaries (`facts`, `distilled`, `chunks_scanned`, `branches`, …) must be **identical** between the two runs (lines 445-450). Per-run: `failed_chunks == 0`, empty `warnings`, timing components ≤ `total_seconds`, `total_agent_calls == extraction + reconcile`, `cache_hits == dry.cached_sessions` (lines 405-434).\\n- **Cache discipline** — unless all three runs set `force`, manifest must declare `cache_state == \\\"cleared_before_each_run\\\"` (lines 398-399).\\n- **`local_ollama_contract`** — `validate_local_ollama_contract` (lines 159-210) requires a retained `go test -json` JSONL whose SHA matches, whose `required_tests`/`command`/`source_paths` equal the hard-coded constants (lines 27-59), whose `source_head` is a 40-char commit, and which actually contains a `pass` event for all 9 named tests plus a package-level pass.\\n\\nRun via `mise run distill:evidence` (per README). CLI: `--manifest`, `--repo-root`, `--out-dir`, `--fail-on-flags` (lines 536-557).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. The existing retained evidence (`evidence/distill-perf/`)\\n\\n**What/where/which model.** `manifest.json` target is `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain` (`repo_key gh/ashtom/entire-brain`), `source_head d7a59688…`, `claim_scope: \\\"current-repo local command-agent distill extraction scheduling speedup\\\"`. `min_speedup: 1.25`, `cache_state: \\\"force_recomputed_each_run\\\"` (all runs `--force`).\\n\\nThe three timed/dry artifacts were produced with **`--agent command` running `python3 local-command-agent.py`** — a deterministic, offline, no-model stand-in — at `--max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75`, on a **temp copy** of this repo's brain store (`dry-run.json` `brain_path: /tmp/pr33-evidence-data/repos/gh/ashtom/entire-brain`).\\n\\nMeasured (dry-run.json): 158 sessions, 0 cached, 185 chunks, raw 379,742,189 B → preprocessed 11,748,560 B, est ≤ 370 agent calls. Both timed runs (jobs-1.json / jobs-4.json) produce **identical** output: 185 facts, 185 extraction + 150 reconcile = 335 total agent calls. Timing:\\n- `jobs-1`: `total_seconds 18.492`, `extraction_wait_seconds 13.510`\\n- `jobs-4`: `total_seconds 5.860`, `extraction_wait_seconds 1.091`\\n\\n`distill-perf-audit-report.md`: **Status PASS**, release_evidence **true**, observed speedup **3.156x** (≥ 1.25x), 6/6 source hashes, 9/9 Ollama tests.\\n\\n**Provenance / limitations the README is explicit about** (README lines 40-48, manifest `notes` 117-122):\\n- Claim scope is **intentionally narrow** — local command-agent scheduling speedup only. The local agent \\\"does not validate fact quality or hosted-model latency.\\\"\\n- \\\"The committed current-repo artifacts **must not be reused to support a frontend/entire.io 24h distill claim**. That claim still needs retained dry-run and timed artifacts from the target large session repo.\\\"\\n- `go-test-internal-cli-ollama-distill.jsonl` is a **wiring/no-egress safety contract only**, \\\"not evidence that any specific Ollama model produces good facts\\\" (README 45-48; manifest `local_ollama_contract.claim_scope` line 114).\\n- `redactions` (manifest 123-126): brain temp path and person-named branch labels redacted.\\n\\n`local-command-agent.py` itself (lines 46-60): reads stdin; on a `CANDIDATES\\\\n` prompt it emits reconcile decisions, otherwise `time.sleep(0.04)` then emits one deterministic fact line keyed by a sha256 of the chunk. No network, no model — purely exercises scheduler/extraction/reconcile/write mechanics and timing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. The Go CLI distill command (`internal/cli/distill_cmd.go`)\\n\\n**Flags** — `newDistillCommand` (lines 473-504). Relevant ones:\\n- `--dry-run` → `distillOpts.dryRun`, help: **\\\"Estimate distill work without calling an agent or writing facts\\\"** (line 499).\\n- `--jobs` → `distillOpts.jobs`, default 0, **\\\"Compatibility alias for --concurrency\\\"** (line 501); `--concurrency` is the real knob (default `defaultDistillConcurrency = 4`, line 500/51).\\n- `--agent` (default `auto`: `auto, codex, claude-code, ollama, or command`, line 494), `--agent-command`, `--model`, `--effort`, `--max-chunk-bytes` (default `48*1024`), `--confidence`, `--branch`, `--session`, `--force`, `--json`.\\n\\n**`--jobs` semantics** (`runDistill`, lines 524-532): if set, must be > 0; conflicts with an explicit `--concurrency` unless equal; otherwise `concurrency = jobs`. Effective parallelism is reported as `extraction_jobs_cap = min(jobs, work)` (`distillEffectiveExtractionJobs`, lines 1148-1157) — this is the field the auditor checks is `1` (serial) vs `>1` (parallel).\\n\\n**Is `--dry-run` deterministic/offline (no model)? YES.** In `runDistill` the dry-run branch (lines 548-558) calls `buildDistillDryRunReport` and returns **before** any agent runner is constructed:\\n```go\\nif distillOpts.dryRun {\\n    report, err := buildDistillDryRunReport(storage.BrainDir, distillOpts, opts.Now().UTC())\\n    ...\\n    if distillOpts.json { return writeJSON(cmd, report) }\\n    printDistillDryRunReport(cmd, report); return nil\\n}\\nif distillOpts.agent == \\\"none\\\" { ... }\\nif distillOpts.run == nil { distillOpts.run = defaultDistillAgentRunner(distillOpts.agent) }  // only reached for a real run\\n```\\n`buildDistillDryRunReport` → `buildDistillPlan` (lines 1008-1098, 1173-1238) only reads transcripts, preprocesses, fingerprints, and chunks; it computes counts and never invokes `distillOpts.run`. So `--dry-run` is fully offline and deterministic. (Caveat: the dry-run still resolves `--agent auto` to a real agent name at lines 540-542 so the cache salt matches a real run; that resolution reads PATH but makes no model call.)\\n\\n**Does the timed run require an agent/hosted model? YES for the real product path; NO for the retained evidence path.** A non-dry run builds a runner via `defaultDistillAgentRunner(agent)` (lines 1763-1768): `ollama` → `execOllamaDistillAgent` (HTTP), everything else → `execDistillAgent`, which **shells out** to the agent argv per chunk (lines 1770-1806, `exec.CommandContext(... args[0], args[1:]...)`). The short help is literally `\\\"Distill captured sessions into durable facts (agent-required)\\\"` (line 477) and `--agent none` errors (line 559-561). The retained evidence sidesteps a hosted model by using `--agent command --agent-command python3 …local-command-agent.py`, which `execDistillAgent` runs as an ordinary subprocess — real distill engine, fake/offline \\\"model.\\\"\\n\\n**Ollama path is loopback-only, not \\\"hosted.\\\"** `execOllamaDistillAgent` (lines 1843-1928) POSTs `{model, system, prompt, stream:false}` to `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate`, rejects non-loopback URLs (`isLoopbackHTTPURL`, 1930-1943), pins `tr.Proxy=nil`, `DialContext=loopbackOnlyDialContext` (1945+, resolves and dials only loopback IPs), and a `CheckRedirect` that blocks non-loopback redirects (1892-1897). These are exactly the 9 behaviors the `local_ollama_contract` go-test artifact certifies. `--agent codex`/`claude-code`/`command`/`auto` are the egress-capable agents and are rejected under `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS`/`LOCAL_ONLY` (`agent_policy.go:22-32`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. What `docs/release_press_release.md` requires before calling distill \\\"fast\\\"\\n\\nUnder **\\\"What Must Be Proven Before Public Claims\\\"** (lines 46-48):\\n```\\n- Distill performance on a large session repo, using `distill --dry-run --json`\\n  plus paired timed `--jobs 1` and `--jobs N` JSON runs with matching\\n  cache/timing fields.\\n```\\nThe doc draws the same line the README does:\\n- Line 71: \\\"current distill still supports backfill.\\\"\\n- Line 64: \\\"Large-repo distill timing … still pending.\\\"\\n- Lines 89-90 (Proven locally): only **\\\"distill dry-run sizing, current-repo local command-agent distill scheduler speedup evidence\\\"** is claimed proven.\\n- Lines 97-99 (Pending proof): **\\\"target large-repo/frontend distill timing\\\"** explicitly remains unproven.\\n\\nSo per release discipline, \\\"distill is fast on a large repo\\\" is NOT yet a permitted claim; only the narrow current-repo scheduler-speedup statement is.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Runnable offline vs needs hosted model + large target repo\\n\\n**Fully offline / runnable now (this is what the retained P0.2 evidence is):**\\n- `distill --dry-run --json` (no agent call at all).\\n- Timed `--jobs 1` vs `--jobs N` using `--agent command` + the committed `local-command-agent.py` (deterministic, sleeps 0.04s/chunk, no network).\\n- The `local_ollama_contract` go test (`go test -count=1 -json ./internal/cli -run Test(...)`) — fake loopback Ollama, no real model.\\n- `audit_distill_perf.py` / `mise run distill:evidence`.\\n\\n**Needs a hosted model + a large target repo (NOT yet done — the open P0.2 work):**\\n- The press release's \\\"large session repo\\\" timing claim requires paired `--jobs 1`/`--jobs N` runs with a **real agent** (`--agent codex`/`claude-code`, or local `--agent ollama` for the no-egress story) on the actual large/frontend repo, with a new `target` block (its own `source_head` + `brain_manifest_sha256`) and `claim_scope` widened beyond \\\"current-repo local command-agent.\\\" The current artifacts are explicitly forbidden from backing that claim.\\n\\n**Uncertainties:** I did not run the auditor or go tests (read-only recon) — the PASS verdict and 3.156x are taken from the committed `distill-perf-audit-report.md`/`.json`, not re-derived. The `min_speedup` of 1.25 is the manifest's floor for *this* narrow claim; the press release does not pin a numeric speedup bar for the large-repo claim — it only mandates the paired-artifact methodology with matching cache/timing fields.\\n\\nKey file paths:\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py`\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/{manifest.json,dry-run.json,jobs-1.json,jobs-4.json,local-command-agent.py,go-test-internal-cli-ollama-distill.jsonl,README.md,distill-perf-audit-report.{json,md}}`\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` (newDistillCommand 473, runDistill 506, dry-run branch 548, jobs logic 524, runners 1763-1928)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill.go` (distillAgentCommandArgs 105, ollama argv 119, injectAgentModel 133)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_policy.go` (rejectAgentForNoEgress 22)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md` (lines 46-48, 64-71, 89-99)\"\n25\t    },\n26\t    {\n27\t      \"subsystem\": \"ledger-gates\",\n28\t      \"map\": \"I now have a complete, citeable map of the subsystem.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# EVAL-LEDGER STANDARD + RELEASE MATRIX / CI GATES — Subsystem Map\\n\\nNote on repo state: the checkout is now on branch `claude/proof-gap-replay-distill` (the codex agent shares this working tree; the original `git status` showed many `audit_*.py` files as `D` because of an in-progress merge/stash, but all target files are present on disk and were read live — confirmed via `ls`/`wc`). Line numbers below are from the on-disk files.\\n\\n## 1. The eval-ledger standard\\n\\nTwo docs carry the standard:\\n\\n**`docs/eval_ledger.md`** — the ledger structure and the comparability rule (eval_ledger.md:3-7):\\n> \\\"One row per retrieval-quality measurement that gated a decision... **numbers are comparable only within a row's own baseline**, never across rows. Before claiming a regression or a win, find the row whose gate you are re-testing and reproduce its exact config; the source doc has the repro commands.\\\"\\n\\nEach row's required fields are the table columns (eval_ledger.md:9): `Date | Corpus / tasks | Comparison | Headline | Decision it gated | Source`. \\\"Adding a row\\\" (eval_ledger.md:52-55) makes them mandatory and same-day:\\n> \\\"date, corpus + task count, what was compared, the headline number with its significance, the decision it served, and where the repro lives.\\\"\\n\\nThere is also a **\\\"Closed negatives — do not re-litigate without new evidence\\\"** section (eval_ledger.md:26-49) with an explicit reopening discipline (eval_ledger.md:33-34): \\\"Closed negatives are reopened by new consumers or new measurements, never by forgetting why they closed.\\\"\\n\\n**The \\\"no euphemism\\\" phrasing itself lives in `docs/release-blockers.md:5-6`** (which inherits the ledger's standard):\\n> \\\"The standard for this file is the eval ledger's: explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\\\"\\n\\n(Uncertain: `docs/eval_ledger.md` does not contain the literal words \\\"explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism\\\" — that exact triplet appears only in `release-blockers.md:6`, attributed to the ledger. The ledger encodes the same standard procedurally via the within-row-only and same-day-row-with-significance rules.)\\n\\n## 2. `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py`\\n\\nThis is a **claim-hygiene gate, not a release-ready declaration** (module docstring, lines 3-8):\\n> \\\"It verifies that every release-readiness ask is either backed by retained evidence or explicitly retained as no-claim / pending evidence, so docs and CI cannot accidentally promote an unsupported claim.\\\"\\n\\n**What it checks.** It loads a manifest (validated at lines 84-98: `schema==1`, required keys `repo_root`/`reports`/`docs`/`mise`), then aggregates 5 referenced JSON reports + `mise.toml` + the press-release doc into ~10 \\\"tracks\\\" (rows), each with `status`, `claimable`, `evidence`, `detail`, `flags`. The tracks:\\n\\n- **replay-lab retained agent proof** (lines 125-164) — branches on `claim_policy`.\\n- **QMD/Radar tool contract** (166-184) — requires `ok==True`, `claim_scope==\\\"mcp_radar_tool_contract\\\"`, and a retained \\\"QMD\\\"/\\\"brain_search\\\" claim.\\n- **distill local scheduler** (186-200) + **target large-repo distill = `pending-target-evidence`, claimable=False** (201-208).\\n- **facts vs raw** (210-242) — branches on `no_release_claim` vs `proof_required`.\\n- **workspace Radar agent lift** (244-262) — hard-pinned to `no_release_claim`, `claimable=False`.\\n- **semantic freshness** (264-277, requires `mise` task `semantic:evidence` exists and is wired into `release:readiness`) + **semantic usefulness = `pending-retained-proof`** (278-285).\\n- **release narrative** (287-303) — press-release must contain required headings and every `required_press_guardrails` phrase.\\n- **single local release-readiness gate** (305-321) — every `required_mise_tasks` entry must be defined and (except itself) referenced inside `release:readiness`'s run block.\\n\\n**`no_release_claim` mode** (release track, lines 131-143): when the release report's `claim_policy == \\\"no_release_claim\\\"`, it asserts the report is *consistently* no-claim and flags any contradiction:\\n```python\\nif release_claim_policy == \\\"no_release_claim\\\":\\n    if release_gate.get(\\\"status\\\") != \\\"pass\\\":\\n        release_flags.append(\\\"release no-claim audit gate is not passing\\\")\\n    if release_gate.get(\\\"release_evidence\\\") is True:\\n        release_flags.append(\\\"release no-claim audit unexpectedly marks release_evidence true\\\")\\n    if int(release_totals.get(\\\"proof_ready_comparisons\\\") or 0) != 0:\\n        release_flags.append(\\\"release no-claim audit unexpectedly retains proof-ready comparisons\\\")\\n    release_status = \\\"no-claim\\\"\\n    release_claimable = False\\n```\\nSo no-claim mode means: evidence is retained and audit-clean, but the track is **not claimable** and must have **zero proof-ready comparisons**. The auditor's job is to catch a no-claim report that \\\"leaks\\\" a claim.\\n\\n**Overall verdict** (lines 323-343): `status = \\\"fail\\\" if flags else \\\"pass\\\"`, and crucially `release_fully_ready` is **hardcoded `False`** (line 333) — the matrix never asserts full readiness. `claimable` tracks are those with `row[\\\"claimable\\\"] == True`; everything else is no-claim/pending. The CLI returns nonzero only with `--fail-on-flags` set (lines 401-402).\\n\\n## 3. CI / mise wiring — which auditors run and what gates a claim\\n\\n**CI: `.github/workflows/test.yml`, `release-evidence` job (lines 89-184).** It runs `run_test.py` then 7 auditors, each `--fail-on-flags` / `--fail-when-no-proof`, then byte-compares the freshly generated reports against the committed ones with `cmp -s` (stale = fail). The auditors, in order: `audit_codex.py`, `audit_radar_evidence.py`, `audit_radar_tool_evidence.py`, `audit_workspace_radar_evidence.py`, `audit_distill_perf.py`, `audit_facts_eval.py`, `audit_release_matrix.py`. Example gate (workflow lines 127-139):\\n```yaml\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py \\\\\\n  --manifest benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/manifest.json \\\\\\n  --out-dir \\\"$tmp\\\" --fail-on-flags\\n...\\nif ! cmp -s \\\"$committed\\\" \\\"$generated\\\"; then\\n  echo \\\"retained release matrix report is stale: $report\\\" >&2\\n```\\n\\n**mise: `mise.toml`.** The single aggregate gate is `release:readiness` (lines 444-467), which loops every sub-gate and fails if any fails:\\n```sh\\nfor task in check release:evidence radar:evidence radar:agent-evidence \\\\\\n            workspace-radar:evidence distill:evidence facts:evidence \\\\\\n            semantic:evidence release:matrix; do\\n  mise run \\\"$task\\\"\\n```\\nEach `*:evidence` task is **check-only** (audits + `cmp -s` staleness, never rewrites), with a paired `*:evidence:update` task that regenerates the committed report after the gate passes. E.g. `release:matrix` (lines 396-422) audits `--fail-on-flags` and then `cmp -s` against the committed `release-matrix-report.{json,md}`, printing `run: mise run release:matrix:update` on drift.\\n\\n**The command that refuses non-proof-ready evidence from becoming a claim** is `audit_codex.py`'s gate, invoked by `release:evidence` (mise.toml:22-44) and `radar:agent-evidence` (mise.toml:140-172). The `radar:agent-evidence` task hard-asserts the no-claim contract inline:\\n```python\\nif policy != \\\"no_release_claim\\\": ...\\nif gate.get(\\\"release_evidence\\\") is not False:\\n    print(\\\"radar agent no-claim gate must not be release evidence\\\", ...)\\nif proof_ready != 0:\\n    print(\\\"radar agent no-claim gate must have zero proof-ready comparisons\\\", ...)\\n```\\n(`semantic:evidence`, mise.toml:358-394, is the one *live* gate — it runs `entire-brain status --json --fail-on release` against the actual indexed brain, so it cannot be satisfied by a stale retained file.)\\n\\n## 4. Registration flow — how a new proof flips a claim from forbidden to allowed\\n\\nThe forbidden/allowed decision is driven entirely by the per-lane **`manifest.json`'s `claim_policy`** plus the proof-ready counters that `audit_codex.py` computes from `summary.json` files.\\n\\n**Current state — everything is forbidden by manifest.** Every retained lane manifest currently declares `\\\"claim_policy\\\": \\\"no_release_claim\\\"`:\\n- `evidence/release/manifest.json`: `claim_policy: no_release_claim`, `minimums.proof_ready_comparisons: 0`, `required_proof_scopes: []`, with a `quarantine_note` that the B1 clean reruns are audit-clean but \\\"no retained replay-lab comparison is proof-ready.\\\"\\n- `evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json` and `evidence/workspace-radar/manifest.json`: both `no_release_claim`, with quarantine notes saying paired/stronger proof is still required.\\n\\n**The flip mechanism** is in `audit_codex.py:build_gate_status` (lines 1325-1413):\\n- Under `no_release_claim` (1349-1370): `release_evidence` is forced `False` and any `proof_ready_comparisons > 0` becomes a *failure* (line 1354-1355). Retained evidence stays non-citable by construction.\\n- Under `proof_required` (1371-1413): it requires `proof_ready >= min_proof_ready`, MCP-verified minimums, `hard_flags == 0`, and that every `required_proof_scopes` / `required_named_tool_proof_scopes` has `> 0` proof-ready comparisons; only then `release_evidence = not failures` (line 1399).\\n\\nA comparison only counts as `proof_ready` if it survives the integrity gate in `audit_summary` (audit_codex.py:986-989): it needs N≥`min_repetitions_per_side` on both arms and `stability.tag == \\\"brain_positive_stable\\\"`, else it gets flags `G:proof_ready_without_n4` / `G:proof_ready_without_stable_gate`.\\n\\n**So the end-to-end registration flow is:**\\n1. Produce a clean replay-lab suite (`run_test.py` / `run.py`) named to match the manifest's `release_citable_suite_globs` (`release-candidate-*`), surviving `brain_query_leak_audit` (release-blockers.md:24-27).\\n2. Copy it into `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/` and **edit the lane manifest**: switch `claim_policy` from `no_release_claim` to `proof_required`, raise `minimums.proof_ready_comparisons`, and add `required_proof_scopes` (e.g. `history`, `mcp`, `mcp_radar_location_only` per the release-matrix manifest's `required_release_proof_scopes`).\\n3. Run `mise run release:evidence:update` (mise.toml:46-60) to regenerate the committed `codex-audit-report.{json,md}`; then `mise run release:matrix:update` (mise.toml:424-442) to regenerate `release-matrix-report.{json,md}` — the matrix row now reads `proven` / `claimable=true` instead of `no-claim`.\\n4. Add the row to `docs/eval_ledger.md` the same day (eval_ledger.md:52-55), update `docs/release_press_release.md` (it must keep the required headings and guardrail phrases the matrix checks at audit_release_matrix.py:288-294).\\n5. CI's `release-evidence` job re-runs every auditor and `cmp -s` the committed reports; if the regenerated reports don't match byte-for-byte, the build fails as \\\"stale\\\" — so the manifest change, the regenerated reports, and the doc updates must all be committed together.\\n\\n**Key files (all absolute):**\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/eval_ledger.md` (the ledger + closed-negatives discipline)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release-blockers.md` (lines 5-6: the \\\"explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism\\\" standard)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md` (lines 73-97: \\\"Future Claims We Should Not Make Yet\\\" + \\\"Release Checklist\\\" — the headings the matrix enforces)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py` (the matrix auditor)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py` (lines 1325-1413 `build_gate_status`, 968-999 `audit_summary` proof-ready gate — the engine behind no-claim vs proof_required)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/manifest.json` and `README.md`\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/{release,facts-eval,workspace-radar}/manifest.json` (all `claim_policy: no_release_claim` today)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml` (tasks at lines 22-60, 358-467: `release:evidence(:update)`, `semantic:evidence`, `release:matrix(:update)`, `release:readiness`)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/.github/workflows/test.yml` (lines 89-184: the `release-evidence` CI job)\"\n29\t    }\n30\t  ]\n31\t}"}]},"uuid":"d186b61f-2c97-43f7-b967-e0a6238738b8","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:16:23.949Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/w5fk2l6k1.output","content":"    },\n    {\n      \"subsystem\": \"distill-perf\",\n      \"map\": \"I now have a complete picture. Here is the deliverable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# DISTILL PERFORMANCE PROOF (P0.2) — Subsystem Map\\n\\nNote on git state: the prompt's git status lists these files as `D` (deleted), but they are **present on disk** in the working tree (`benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py`, all `evidence/distill-perf/*`, all `internal/cli/distill*.go`). The status snapshot is stale; everything below was read from the live files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. The auditor: `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py`\\n\\n**Evidence shape it expects** — a `manifest.json` (`schema == 1`) pointing at three sibling JSON artifacts plus a retained go-test artifact. Top-level validation (`validate_manifest`, lines 113-129) requires: `target` object, the three relative-path fields `dry_run`/`serial_run`/`parallel_run`, an `artifact_sha256` map, and a `commands` map.\\n\\n**What makes evidence PASS/FAIL** — `status` is `\\\"fail\\\"` if any flag is appended, else `\\\"pass\\\"`; `release_evidence` is `not flags` (audit_distill_perf.py:466-467). Key gates:\\n\\n- **Speedup gate (the \\\"fast\\\" bar)** — `min_speedup` must be `> 1.0` (raises if not, line 452-454). Observed speedup = `serial.total_seconds / parallel.total_seconds`; flagged if below threshold (lines 455-459):\\n  ```python\\n  speedup = float(serial[\\\"total_seconds\\\"]) / float(parallel[\\\"total_seconds\\\"])\\n  if speedup < float(min_speedup):\\n      flags.append(f\\\"speedup {speedup:.3f} < required {float(min_speedup):.3f}\\\")\\n  ```\\n- **Artifact + source integrity** — every JSON artifact's SHA-256 must match `artifact_sha256.*` (lines 303-311); every file in `DISTILL_PERF_SOURCE_PATHS` (the 4 `distill*.go` files + this auditor + `local-command-agent.py`, lines 22-26) must match `source_sha256` and exist under repo root (lines 314-335).\\n- **Dry-run shape** — `schema_version == 1`; a list of positive-number fields (`sessions`, `chunks`, `extraction_agent_calls`, …) at line 375; `missing_transcripts == 0`; empty `warnings`; `chunks == extraction_agent_calls`; `estimated_agent_calls_upper_bound == extraction + reconcile upper bound`; non-empty `branches` and `largest_sessions`; branch field sums must equal totals (`validate_branch_sums`, lines 338-345).\\n- **Command provenance** — `validate_command` (lines 273-300) requires each retained `commands.*` token list to contain `distill` and `--json`, the dry-run list to contain `--dry-run`, an **explicit `--agent` (not `\\\"\\\"`/`auto`)**, and `--model`/`--effort`/`--branch`/`--jobs`/`--max-chunk-bytes`/`--confidence` to **match the artifact's recorded fields**.\\n- **Serial vs parallel equivalence** — same agent/model/branch/force/chunk/confidence config (`config_tuple`, lines 236-245, checked at 401-404); `serial.jobs == 1`, `serial.extraction_jobs_cap ∈ {0,1}`; `parallel.jobs > 1` and `extraction_jobs_cap > 1` (lines 436-443); the output summaries (`facts`, `distilled`, `chunks_scanned`, `branches`, …) must be **identical** between the two runs (lines 445-450). Per-run: `failed_chunks == 0`, empty `warnings`, timing components ≤ `total_seconds`, `total_agent_calls == extraction + reconcile`, `cache_hits == dry.cached_sessions` (lines 405-434).\\n- **Cache discipline** — unless all three runs set `force`, manifest must declare `cache_state == \\\"cleared_before_each_run\\\"` (lines 398-399).\\n- **`local_ollama_contract`** — `validate_local_ollama_contract` (lines 159-210) requires a retained `go test -json` JSONL whose SHA matches, whose `required_tests`/`command`/`source_paths` equal the hard-coded constants (lines 27-59), whose `source_head` is a 40-char commit, and which actually contains a `pass` event for all 9 named tests plus a package-level pass.\\n\\nRun via `mise run distill:evidence` (per README). CLI: `--manifest`, `--repo-root`, `--out-dir`, `--fail-on-flags` (lines 536-557).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. The existing retained evidence (`evidence/distill-perf/`)\\n\\n**What/where/which model.** `manifest.json` target is `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain` (`repo_key gh/ashtom/entire-brain`), `source_head d7a59688…`, `claim_scope: \\\"current-repo local command-agent distill extraction scheduling speedup\\\"`. `min_speedup: 1.25`, `cache_state: \\\"force_recomputed_each_run\\\"` (all runs `--force`).\\n\\nThe three timed/dry artifacts were produced with **`--agent command` running `python3 local-command-agent.py`** — a deterministic, offline, no-model stand-in — at `--max-chunk-bytes 262144 --confidence 0.75`, on a **temp copy** of this repo's brain store (`dry-run.json` `brain_path: /tmp/pr33-evidence-data/repos/gh/ashtom/entire-brain`).\\n\\nMeasured (dry-run.json): 158 sessions, 0 cached, 185 chunks, raw 379,742,189 B → preprocessed 11,748,560 B, est ≤ 370 agent calls. Both timed runs (jobs-1.json / jobs-4.json) produce **identical** output: 185 facts, 185 extraction + 150 reconcile = 335 total agent calls. Timing:\\n- `jobs-1`: `total_seconds 18.492`, `extraction_wait_seconds 13.510`\\n- `jobs-4`: `total_seconds 5.860`, `extraction_wait_seconds 1.091`\\n\\n`distill-perf-audit-report.md`: **Status PASS**, release_evidence **true**, observed speedup **3.156x** (≥ 1.25x), 6/6 source hashes, 9/9 Ollama tests.\\n\\n**Provenance / limitations the README is explicit about** (README lines 40-48, manifest `notes` 117-122):\\n- Claim scope is **intentionally narrow** — local command-agent scheduling speedup only. The local agent \\\"does not validate fact quality or hosted-model latency.\\\"\\n- \\\"The committed current-repo artifacts **must not be reused to support a frontend/entire.io 24h distill claim**. That claim still needs retained dry-run and timed artifacts from the target large session repo.\\\"\\n- `go-test-internal-cli-ollama-distill.jsonl` is a **wiring/no-egress safety contract only**, \\\"not evidence that any specific Ollama model produces good facts\\\" (README 45-48; manifest `local_ollama_contract.claim_scope` line 114).\\n- `redactions` (manifest 123-126): brain temp path and person-named branch labels redacted.\\n\\n`local-command-agent.py` itself (lines 46-60): reads stdin; on a `CANDIDATES\\\\n` prompt it emits reconcile decisions, otherwise `time.sleep(0.04)` then emits one deterministic fact line keyed by a sha256 of the chunk. No network, no model — purely exercises scheduler/extraction/reconcile/write mechanics and timing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. The Go CLI distill command (`internal/cli/distill_cmd.go`)\\n\\n**Flags** — `newDistillCommand` (lines 473-504). Relevant ones:\\n- `--dry-run` → `distillOpts.dryRun`, help: **\\\"Estimate distill work without calling an agent or writing facts\\\"** (line 499).\\n- `--jobs` → `distillOpts.jobs`, default 0, **\\\"Compatibility alias for --concurrency\\\"** (line 501); `--concurrency` is the real knob (default `defaultDistillConcurrency = 4`, line 500/51).\\n- `--agent` (default `auto`: `auto, codex, claude-code, ollama, or command`, line 494), `--agent-command`, `--model`, `--effort`, `--max-chunk-bytes` (default `48*1024`), `--confidence`, `--branch`, `--session`, `--force`, `--json`.\\n\\n**`--jobs` semantics** (`runDistill`, lines 524-532): if set, must be > 0; conflicts with an explicit `--concurrency` unless equal; otherwise `concurrency = jobs`. Effective parallelism is reported as `extraction_jobs_cap = min(jobs, work)` (`distillEffectiveExtractionJobs`, lines 1148-1157) — this is the field the auditor checks is `1` (serial) vs `>1` (parallel).\\n\\n**Is `--dry-run` deterministic/offline (no model)? YES.** In `runDistill` the dry-run branch (lines 548-558) calls `buildDistillDryRunReport` and returns **before** any agent runner is constructed:\\n```go\\nif distillOpts.dryRun {\\n    report, err := buildDistillDryRunReport(storage.BrainDir, distillOpts, opts.Now().UTC())\\n    ...\\n    if distillOpts.json { return writeJSON(cmd, report) }\\n    printDistillDryRunReport(cmd, report); return nil\\n}\\nif distillOpts.agent == \\\"none\\\" { ... }\\nif distillOpts.run == nil { distillOpts.run = defaultDistillAgentRunner(distillOpts.agent) }  // only reached for a real run\\n```\\n`buildDistillDryRunReport` → `buildDistillPlan` (lines 1008-1098, 1173-1238) only reads transcripts, preprocesses, fingerprints, and chunks; it computes counts and never invokes `distillOpts.run`. So `--dry-run` is fully offline and deterministic. (Caveat: the dry-run still resolves `--agent auto` to a real agent name at lines 540-542 so the cache salt matches a real run; that resolution reads PATH but makes no model call.)\\n\\n**Does the timed run require an agent/hosted model? YES for the real product path; NO for the retained evidence path.** A non-dry run builds a runner via `defaultDistillAgentRunner(agent)` (lines 1763-1768): `ollama` → `execOllamaDistillAgent` (HTTP), everything else → `execDistillAgent`, which **shells out** to the agent argv per chunk (lines 1770-1806, `exec.CommandContext(... args[0], args[1:]...)`). The short help is literally `\\\"Distill captured sessions into durable facts (agent-required)\\\"` (line 477) and `--agent none` errors (line 559-561). The retained evidence sidesteps a hosted model by using `--agent command --agent-command python3 …local-command-agent.py`, which `execDistillAgent` runs as an ordinary subprocess — real distill engine, fake/offline \\\"model.\\\"\\n\\n**Ollama path is loopback-only, not \\\"hosted.\\\"** `execOllamaDistillAgent` (lines 1843-1928) POSTs `{model, system, prompt, stream:false}` to `ENTIRE_BRAIN_OLLAMA_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate`, rejects non-loopback URLs (`isLoopbackHTTPURL`, 1930-1943), pins `tr.Proxy=nil`, `DialContext=loopbackOnlyDialContext` (1945+, resolves and dials only loopback IPs), and a `CheckRedirect` that blocks non-loopback redirects (1892-1897). These are exactly the 9 behaviors the `local_ollama_contract` go-test artifact certifies. `--agent codex`/`claude-code`/`command`/`auto` are the egress-capable agents and are rejected under `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS`/`LOCAL_ONLY` (`agent_policy.go:22-32`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. What `docs/release_press_release.md` requires before calling distill \\\"fast\\\"\\n\\nUnder **\\\"What Must Be Proven Before Public Claims\\\"** (lines 46-48):\\n```\\n- Distill performance on a large session repo, using `distill --dry-run --json`\\n  plus paired timed `--jobs 1` and `--jobs N` JSON runs with matching\\n  cache/timing fields.\\n```\\nThe doc draws the same line the README does:\\n- Line 71: \\\"current distill still supports backfill.\\\"\\n- Line 64: \\\"Large-repo distill timing … still pending.\\\"\\n- Lines 89-90 (Proven locally): only **\\\"distill dry-run sizing, current-repo local command-agent distill scheduler speedup evidence\\\"** is claimed proven.\\n- Lines 97-99 (Pending proof): **\\\"target large-repo/frontend distill timing\\\"** explicitly remains unproven.\\n\\nSo per release discipline, \\\"distill is fast on a large repo\\\" is NOT yet a permitted claim; only the narrow current-repo scheduler-speedup statement is.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Runnable offline vs needs hosted model + large target repo\\n\\n**Fully offline / runnable now (this is what the retained P0.2 evidence is):**\\n- `distill --dry-run --json` (no agent call at all).\\n- Timed `--jobs 1` vs `--jobs N` using `--agent command` + the committed `local-command-agent.py` (deterministic, sleeps 0.04s/chunk, no network).\\n- The `local_ollama_contract` go test (`go test -count=1 -json ./internal/cli -run Test(...)`) — fake loopback Ollama, no real model.\\n- `audit_distill_perf.py` / `mise run distill:evidence`.\\n\\n**Needs a hosted model + a large target repo (NOT yet done — the open P0.2 work):**\\n- The press release's \\\"large session repo\\\" timing claim requires paired `--jobs 1`/`--jobs N` runs with a **real agent** (`--agent codex`/`claude-code`, or local `--agent ollama` for the no-egress story) on the actual large/frontend repo, with a new `target` block (its own `source_head` + `brain_manifest_sha256`) and `claim_scope` widened beyond \\\"current-repo local command-agent.\\\" The current artifacts are explicitly forbidden from backing that claim.\\n\\n**Uncertainties:** I did not run the auditor or go tests (read-only recon) — the PASS verdict and 3.156x are taken from the committed `distill-perf-audit-report.md`/`.json`, not re-derived. The `min_speedup` of 1.25 is the manifest's floor for *this* narrow claim; the press release does not pin a numeric speedup bar for the large-repo claim — it only mandates the paired-artifact methodology with matching cache/timing fields.\\n\\nKey file paths:\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py`\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/{manifest.json,dry-run.json,jobs-1.json,jobs-4.json,local-command-agent.py,go-test-internal-cli-ollama-distill.jsonl,README.md,distill-perf-audit-report.{json,md}}`\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill_cmd.go` (newDistillCommand 473, runDistill 506, dry-run branch 548, jobs logic 524, runners 1763-1928)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/distill.go` (distillAgentCommandArgs 105, ollama argv 119, injectAgentModel 133)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_policy.go` (rejectAgentForNoEgress 22)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md` (lines 46-48, 64-71, 89-99)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"subsystem\": \"ledger-gates\",\n      \"map\": \"I now have a complete, citeable map of the subsystem.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# EVAL-LEDGER STANDARD + RELEASE MATRIX / CI GATES — Subsystem Map\\n\\nNote on repo state: the checkout is now on branch `claude/proof-gap-replay-distill` (the codex agent shares this working tree; the original `git status` showed many `audit_*.py` files as `D` because of an in-progress merge/stash, but all target files are present on disk and were read live — confirmed via `ls`/`wc`). Line numbers below are from the on-disk files.\\n\\n## 1. The eval-ledger standard\\n\\nTwo docs carry the standard:\\n\\n**`docs/eval_ledger.md`** — the ledger structure and the comparability rule (eval_ledger.md:3-7):\\n> \\\"One row per retrieval-quality measurement that gated a decision... **numbers are comparable only within a row's own baseline**, never across rows. Before claiming a regression or a win, find the row whose gate you are re-testing and reproduce its exact config; the source doc has the repro commands.\\\"\\n\\nEach row's required fields are the table columns (eval_ledger.md:9): `Date | Corpus / tasks | Comparison | Headline | Decision it gated | Source`. \\\"Adding a row\\\" (eval_ledger.md:52-55) makes them mandatory and same-day:\\n> \\\"date, corpus + task count, what was compared, the headline number with its significance, the decision it served, and where the repro lives.\\\"\\n\\nThere is also a **\\\"Closed negatives — do not re-litigate without new evidence\\\"** section (eval_ledger.md:26-49) with an explicit reopening discipline (eval_ledger.md:33-34): \\\"Closed negatives are reopened by new consumers or new measurements, never by forgetting why they closed.\\\"\\n\\n**The \\\"no euphemism\\\" phrasing itself lives in `docs/release-blockers.md:5-6`** (which inherits the ledger's standard):\\n> \\\"The standard for this file is the eval ledger's: explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\\\"\\n\\n(Uncertain: `docs/eval_ledger.md` does not contain the literal words \\\"explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism\\\" — that exact triplet appears only in `release-blockers.md:6`, attributed to the ledger. The ledger encodes the same standard procedurally via the within-row-only and same-day-row-with-significance rules.)\\n\\n## 2. `benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py`\\n\\nThis is a **claim-hygiene gate, not a release-ready declaration** (module docstring, lines 3-8):\\n> \\\"It verifies that every release-readiness ask is either backed by retained evidence or explicitly retained as no-claim / pending evidence, so docs and CI cannot accidentally promote an unsupported claim.\\\"\\n\\n**What it checks.** It loads a manifest (validated at lines 84-98: `schema==1`, required keys `repo_root`/`reports`/`docs`/`mise`), then aggregates 5 referenced JSON reports + `mise.toml` + the press-release doc into ~10 \\\"tracks\\\" (rows), each with `status`, `claimable`, `evidence`, `detail`, `flags`. The tracks:\\n\\n- **replay-lab retained agent proof** (lines 125-164) — branches on `claim_policy`.\\n- **QMD/Radar tool contract** (166-184) — requires `ok==True`, `claim_scope==\\\"mcp_radar_tool_contract\\\"`, and a retained \\\"QMD\\\"/\\\"brain_search\\\" claim.\\n- **distill local scheduler** (186-200) + **target large-repo distill = `pending-target-evidence`, claimable=False** (201-208).\\n- **facts vs raw** (210-242) — branches on `no_release_claim` vs `proof_required`.\\n- **workspace Radar agent lift** (244-262) — hard-pinned to `no_release_claim`, `claimable=False`.\\n- **semantic freshness** (264-277, requires `mise` task `semantic:evidence` exists and is wired into `release:readiness`) + **semantic usefulness = `pending-retained-proof`** (278-285).\\n- **release narrative** (287-303) — press-release must contain required headings and every `required_press_guardrails` phrase.\\n- **single local release-readiness gate** (305-321) — every `required_mise_tasks` entry must be defined and (except itself) referenced inside `release:readiness`'s run block.\\n\\n**`no_release_claim` mode** (release track, lines 131-143): when the release report's `claim_policy == \\\"no_release_claim\\\"`, it asserts the report is *consistently* no-claim and flags any contradiction:\\n```python\\nif release_claim_policy == \\\"no_release_claim\\\":\\n    if release_gate.get(\\\"status\\\") != \\\"pass\\\":\\n        release_flags.append(\\\"release no-claim audit gate is not passing\\\")\\n    if release_gate.get(\\\"release_evidence\\\") is True:\\n        release_flags.append(\\\"release no-claim audit unexpectedly marks release_evidence true\\\")\\n    if int(release_totals.get(\\\"proof_ready_comparisons\\\") or 0) != 0:\\n        release_flags.append(\\\"release no-claim audit unexpectedly retains proof-ready comparisons\\\")\\n    release_status = \\\"no-claim\\\"\\n    release_claimable = False\\n```\\nSo no-claim mode means: evidence is retained and audit-clean, but the track is **not claimable** and must have **zero proof-ready comparisons**. The auditor's job is to catch a no-claim report that \\\"leaks\\\" a claim.\\n\\n**Overall verdict** (lines 323-343): `status = \\\"fail\\\" if flags else \\\"pass\\\"`, and crucially `release_fully_ready` is **hardcoded `False`** (line 333) — the matrix never asserts full readiness. `claimable` tracks are those with `row[\\\"claimable\\\"] == True`; everything else is no-claim/pending. The CLI returns nonzero only with `--fail-on-flags` set (lines 401-402).\\n\\n## 3. CI / mise wiring — which auditors run and what gates a claim\\n\\n**CI: `.github/workflows/test.yml`, `release-evidence` job (lines 89-184).** It runs `run_test.py` then 7 auditors, each `--fail-on-flags` / `--fail-when-no-proof`, then byte-compares the freshly generated reports against the committed ones with `cmp -s` (stale = fail). The auditors, in order: `audit_codex.py`, `audit_radar_evidence.py`, `audit_radar_tool_evidence.py`, `audit_workspace_radar_evidence.py`, `audit_distill_perf.py`, `audit_facts_eval.py`, `audit_release_matrix.py`. Example gate (workflow lines 127-139):\\n```yaml\\npython3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py \\\\\\n  --manifest benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/manifest.json \\\\\\n  --out-dir \\\"$tmp\\\" --fail-on-flags\\n...\\nif ! cmp -s \\\"$committed\\\" \\\"$generated\\\"; then\\n  echo \\\"retained release matrix report is stale: $report\\\" >&2\\n```\\n\\n**mise: `mise.toml`.** The single aggregate gate is `release:readiness` (lines 444-467), which loops every sub-gate and fails if any fails:\\n```sh\\nfor task in check release:evidence radar:evidence radar:agent-evidence \\\\\\n            workspace-radar:evidence distill:evidence facts:evidence \\\\\\n            semantic:evidence release:matrix; do\\n  mise run \\\"$task\\\"\\n```\\nEach `*:evidence` task is **check-only** (audits + `cmp -s` staleness, never rewrites), with a paired `*:evidence:update` task that regenerates the committed report after the gate passes. E.g. `release:matrix` (lines 396-422) audits `--fail-on-flags` and then `cmp -s` against the committed `release-matrix-report.{json,md}`, printing `run: mise run release:matrix:update` on drift.\\n\\n**The command that refuses non-proof-ready evidence from becoming a claim** is `audit_codex.py`'s gate, invoked by `release:evidence` (mise.toml:22-44) and `radar:agent-evidence` (mise.toml:140-172). The `radar:agent-evidence` task hard-asserts the no-claim contract inline:\\n```python\\nif policy != \\\"no_release_claim\\\": ...\\nif gate.get(\\\"release_evidence\\\") is not False:\\n    print(\\\"radar agent no-claim gate must not be release evidence\\\", ...)\\nif proof_ready != 0:\\n    print(\\\"radar agent no-claim gate must have zero proof-ready comparisons\\\", ...)\\n```\\n(`semantic:evidence`, mise.toml:358-394, is the one *live* gate — it runs `entire-brain status --json --fail-on release` against the actual indexed brain, so it cannot be satisfied by a stale retained file.)\\n\\n## 4. Registration flow — how a new proof flips a claim from forbidden to allowed\\n\\nThe forbidden/allowed decision is driven entirely by the per-lane **`manifest.json`'s `claim_policy`** plus the proof-ready counters that `audit_codex.py` computes from `summary.json` files.\\n\\n**Current state — everything is forbidden by manifest.** Every retained lane manifest currently declares `\\\"claim_policy\\\": \\\"no_release_claim\\\"`:\\n- `evidence/release/manifest.json`: `claim_policy: no_release_claim`, `minimums.proof_ready_comparisons: 0`, `required_proof_scopes: []`, with a `quarantine_note` that the B1 clean reruns are audit-clean but \\\"no retained replay-lab comparison is proof-ready.\\\"\\n- `evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json` and `evidence/workspace-radar/manifest.json`: both `no_release_claim`, with quarantine notes saying paired/stronger proof is still required.\\n\\n**The flip mechanism** is in `audit_codex.py:build_gate_status` (lines 1325-1413):\\n- Under `no_release_claim` (1349-1370): `release_evidence` is forced `False` and any `proof_ready_comparisons > 0` becomes a *failure* (line 1354-1355). Retained evidence stays non-citable by construction.\\n- Under `proof_required` (1371-1413): it requires `proof_ready >= min_proof_ready`, MCP-verified minimums, `hard_flags == 0`, and that every `required_proof_scopes` / `required_named_tool_proof_scopes` has `> 0` proof-ready comparisons; only then `release_evidence = not failures` (line 1399).\\n\\nA comparison only counts as `proof_ready` if it survives the integrity gate in `audit_summary` (audit_codex.py:986-989): it needs N≥`min_repetitions_per_side` on both arms and `stability.tag == \\\"brain_positive_stable\\\"`, else it gets flags `G:proof_ready_without_n4` / `G:proof_ready_without_stable_gate`.\\n\\n**So the end-to-end registration flow is:**\\n1. Produce a clean replay-lab suite (`run_test.py` / `run.py`) named to match the manifest's `release_citable_suite_globs` (`release-candidate-*`), surviving `brain_query_leak_audit` (release-blockers.md:24-27).\\n2. Copy it into `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/` and **edit the lane manifest**: switch `claim_policy` from `no_release_claim` to `proof_required`, raise `minimums.proof_ready_comparisons`, and add `required_proof_scopes` (e.g. `history`, `mcp`, `mcp_radar_location_only` per the release-matrix manifest's `required_release_proof_scopes`).\\n3. Run `mise run release:evidence:update` (mise.toml:46-60) to regenerate the committed `codex-audit-report.{json,md}`; then `mise run release:matrix:update` (mise.toml:424-442) to regenerate `release-matrix-report.{json,md}` — the matrix row now reads `proven` / `claimable=true` instead of `no-claim`.\\n4. Add the row to `docs/eval_ledger.md` the same day (eval_ledger.md:52-55), update `docs/release_press_release.md` (it must keep the required headings and guardrail phrases the matrix checks at audit_release_matrix.py:288-294).\\n5. CI's `release-evidence` job re-runs every auditor and `cmp -s` the committed reports; if the regenerated reports don't match byte-for-byte, the build fails as \\\"stale\\\" — so the manifest change, the regenerated reports, and the doc updates must all be committed together.\\n\\n**Key files (all absolute):**\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/eval_ledger.md` (the ledger + closed-negatives discipline)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release-blockers.md` (lines 5-6: the \\\"explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism\\\" standard)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/docs/release_press_release.md` (lines 73-97: \\\"Future Claims We Should Not Make Yet\\\" + \\\"Release Checklist\\\" — the headings the matrix enforces)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py` (the matrix auditor)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_codex.py` (lines 1325-1413 `build_gate_status`, 968-999 `audit_summary` proof-ready gate — the engine behind no-claim vs proof_required)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/manifest.json` and `README.md`\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/{release,facts-eval,workspace-radar}/manifest.json` (all `claim_policy: no_release_claim` today)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml` (tasks at lines 22-60, 358-467: `release:evidence(:update)`, `semantic:evidence`, `release:matrix(:update)`, `release:readiness`)\\n- `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/.github/workflows/test.yml` (lines 89-184: the `release-evidence` CI job)\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","numLines":11,"startLine":21,"totalLines":31}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"40e07231-c205-4a20-8d05-caecb94fd1e9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
