{"parentUuid":"5763f019-2b1e-4397-8aeb-338bcdc13eae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UDxp6tnCCa9CbvEj3BbJ8W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SLZ8RreC6v3GjvRqpfFYU3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain\necho \"=== eval_ledger: distill / scheduler mentions ===\"\ngrep -n -i \"distill\\|scheduler\\|speedup\\|jobs\" docs/eval_ledger.md || echo \"(no distill rows — eval_ledger is retrieval-quality only)\"\necho \"=== eval_ledger header/table format ===\"\nsed -n '1,12p' docs/eval_ledger.md 2>/dev/null | head -12","description":"Check if distill perf is tracked in eval_ledger"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":374680,"output_tokens":825,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":301,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":374680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":301},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcBA5jn9TqRVoifRViDoW","type":"assistant","uuid":"347d4b8f-b648-4f84-9c78-554be8dbc5a2","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:57:18.056Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"347d4b8f-b648-4f84-9c78-554be8dbc5a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"730c809c-0f0c-4fd9-82a6-805198299ca1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SLZ8RreC6v3GjvRqpfFYU3","type":"tool_result","content":"=== eval_ledger: distill / scheduler mentions ===\n(no distill rows — eval_ledger is retrieval-quality only)\n=== eval_ledger header/table format ===\n# Eval ledger\n\nOne row per retrieval-quality measurement that gated a decision. The task sets,\ncorpus snapshots, and metrics differ between rows — **numbers are comparable\nonly within a row's own baseline**, never across rows. Before claiming a\nregression or a win, find the row whose gate you are re-testing and reproduce\nits exact config; the source doc has the repro commands.\n\n| Date | Corpus / tasks | Comparison | Headline | Decision it gated | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain `main`, 179 facts, 16 provenance-labeled tasks (`facts eval-gen`, k=10) | lexical-only vs Model2Vec fused | lexical 0.86 → fused **1.50 useful/1k** (+76%); concept stratum 0 → 0.79 | Frozen Stage 0 baseline; any later embedder swap must beat 1.50 on this set. Also: facts FTS5 BM25 measured at parity (1.43), so BM25 ships **opt-in** (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BM25=1`), not default | `../alignment.md` (Stage 0); artifacts at `<brain>/eval/baseline-20260608/` |\n| 2026-06-08 | same 16-task set | Model2Vec fused vs EmbeddingGemma-300M (Q8_0, shell-to-local-server runner) | **1.80 useful/1k (+20%)**, precision 0.106, concept stratum 1.68 (2.1×); gain is reachability (three 0.00→~1.75 rescues), not uniform lift | Stage 1b embedder **quality gate: passed**. Runtime/distribution work still parked | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1b) |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a4ff7634-fc4e-46c7-adfa-6ed95ef15912","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:57:18.121Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== eval_ledger: distill / scheduler mentions ===\n(no distill rows — eval_ledger is retrieval-quality only)\n=== eval_ledger header/table format ===\n# Eval ledger\n\nOne row per retrieval-quality measurement that gated a decision. The task sets,\ncorpus snapshots, and metrics differ between rows — **numbers are comparable\nonly within a row's own baseline**, never across rows. Before claiming a\nregression or a win, find the row whose gate you are re-testing and reproduce\nits exact config; the source doc has the repro commands.\n\n| Date | Corpus / tasks | Comparison | Headline | Decision it gated | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain `main`, 179 facts, 16 provenance-labeled tasks (`facts eval-gen`, k=10) | lexical-only vs Model2Vec fused | lexical 0.86 → fused **1.50 useful/1k** (+76%); concept stratum 0 → 0.79 | Frozen Stage 0 baseline; any later embedder swap must beat 1.50 on this set. Also: facts FTS5 BM25 measured at parity (1.43), so BM25 ships **opt-in** (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BM25=1`), not default | `../alignment.md` (Stage 0); artifacts at `<brain>/eval/baseline-20260608/` |\n| 2026-06-08 | same 16-task set | Model2Vec fused vs EmbeddingGemma-300M (Q8_0, shell-to-local-server runner) | **1.80 useful/1k (+20%)**, precision 0.106, concept stratum 1.68 (2.1×); gain is reachability (three 0.00→~1.75 rescues), not uniform lift | Stage 1b embedder **quality gate: passed**. Runtime/distribution work still parked | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1b) |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"347d4b8f-b648-4f84-9c78-554be8dbc5a2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"a4ff7634-fc4e-46c7-adfa-6ed95ef15912","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"64","subject":"P0.2 offline: large-repo distill timing on entireio/cli","description":"Run `distill --dry-run --json` (offline) on the entireio/cli large corpus (822 sessions / 1.6G) for real large-repo sizing, plus paired timed --jobs 1 vs --jobs N via --agent command + local-command-agent (deterministic, no model) on a temp brain copy. Produces dry-run.json/jobs-1.json/jobs-N.json with matching cache/timing fields. No hosted-model usage.","activeForm":"Running offline large-repo distill timing","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"65","subject":"P0.2: build distill-perf manifest + pass audit_distill_perf.py","description":"Author a new evidence manifest with a target block for github.com/entireio/cli and widened claim_scope (large-repo command-agent scheduler speedup), retain artifacts + go-test ollama contract, run audit_distill_perf.py to PASS. Then update press release Proven/Pending lines + eval_ledger row + regenerate release-matrix distill track. Honest scope: command-agent measures scheduler parallelism; note hosted-model latency is separate.","activeForm":"Building distill-perf manifest and passing the auditor","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"66","subject":"P0.1 author: harder/clean correctness-axis replay-lab tasks","description":"Author 3-5 candidate tasks where the decisive answer lives in the brain (history rationale / durable fact / semantic locator) and is NOT recoverable from the repo in budget, so no_brain fails (<100%) and brain reliably passes (100%) → clean correctness_win at n>=4. Symptom-level brain_queries (pass brain_query_leak_audit), hide validation+expected, leak_markers + agent_hidden_paths, pinned base_commit. Templates from existing tasks/*.json.","activeForm":"Authoring harder/clean replay-lab tasks","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"67","subject":"P0.1 offline-validate: leak-audit clean + fails-as-expected + panel","description":"For each candidate task: run `run.py check` (offline, no model) to confirm the regression fails-as-expected, and confirm brain_query_leak_audit passes (no answer-bearing identifiers/phrases). Iterate JSON until clean. Build a panel JSON sized for n>=4-8/side. All offline — no hosted-model usage.","activeForm":"Offline-validating tasks (leak-audit + fails-as-expected)","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"68","subject":"P0.1 (post-2PM): run pilots → scale n>=4-8 → check proof_ready","description":"HOSTED-MODEL, run only after 2 PM limit reset. Run no_brain difficulty pilots (confirm baseline fails / score <90), then brain-arm direction pilots, drop saturated tasks, scale survivors to n>=4-8/side, let run.py compute proof_ready. Drives the session-authed claude/codex CLI.","activeForm":"Running pilots and scaling to proof-ready n","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"69","subject":"P0.1 (post-2PM): register genuine proofs or honest negative","description":"If a suite genuinely flips proof_ready: copy into evidence/release/ matching release_citable_suite_globs, flip manifest claim_policy no_release_claim→proof_required with required_proof_scopes, regenerate codex-audit + release-matrix reports, add eval_ledger row, update press release. If it does NOT flip: document the honest negative finding + what was learned. NEVER fabricate numbers.","activeForm":"Registering genuine proofs (or honest negative)","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"70","subject":"Loop-audit until clean (bugbot-proof)","description":"go build/vet/test/gofmt clean; run full `mise run release:readiness` (all auditors + cmp staleness) green; adversarial self-review workflow over new tasks/manifests/docs for leakage, provenance gaps, stale reports, doc-claim mismatches, schema typos, no person-names; loop until dry. Review-before-push (do not push without user review).","activeForm":"Loop-auditing until no issues remain","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"71","subject":"P0.2 wiring: matrix track + mise + CI + press release + ledger","description":"Wire the large-repo distill lane: make audit_release_matrix.py \"target large-repo distill\" track read the new report and flip to proven (scoped to command-agent scheduler speedup at scale); add reports.distill_large to the release-matrix manifest; add mise distill:large:evidence(+:update) into release:readiness; add CI auditor+cmp; update press release Proven/Pending lines; add eval_ledger row. Flag the stale ollama-contract (tests removed from code) finding.","activeForm":"Wiring the large-repo distill lane into matrix/mise/CI/docs","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":8},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d113909a-ab19-48b3-9470-4832997389b6","timestamp":"2026-06-18T17:57:18.160Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
