{"parentUuid":"e42386b0-644f-4584-8acb-8e7908353b7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011a8rknkQ25u5w5h14XK9av","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the P0.1 authoring workflow — 4 agents, distinct archetypes, each reading real code + verifying the decisive answer is in history."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3985,"cache_read_input_tokens":399199,"output_tokens":4113,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3985,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4113,"cache_read_input_tokens":399199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3985},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcBAYNXTiHFT6QSTTLm81","type":"assistant","uuid":"e01ab203-983d-466a-84fe-5e417da2d44b","timestamp":"2026-06-18T18:03:19.938Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"e01ab203-983d-466a-84fe-5e417da2d44b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011a8rknkQ25u5w5h14XK9av","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PToyay2wveCWVrpoSFgYfb","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'p01-author-tasks',\n  description: 'Author 4 clean, harder replay-lab tasks (correctness-axis gap) from distinct archetypes, each verified against real entire-brain code + history',\n  phases: [{ title: 'Author', detail: 'one clean task per archetype' }],\n}\n\nphase('Author')\n\nconst REPO = '/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain'\nconst BIN = '/tmp/entire-brain-proofgap'\nconst BASE = 'fc65f656615f4623a2370ec7943f8d575714cfe8'\n\nconst shared = `You are authoring ONE benchmark task for the entire-brain replay-lab (repo: ${REPO}). READ-ONLY except you return a task JSON as text (do not write files).\n\nTHE GOAL — a \"clean correctness gap\": a task where an agent WITHOUT the brain reliably FAILS validation (pass-rate < 100%) but an agent WITH the brain (history channel) reliably PASSES (100%). The proof gate needs: brain arm 100% pass, no_brain arm < 100%, success_delta > 0 (correctness_win), at n>=4 reps/side. Pass-rate lift only needs to survive drop-one (no p-value), so a CLEAR gap at n=4-8 is enough.\n\nWHY GAPS USUALLY FAIL (avoid these):\n- Saturation: if no_brain can solve it from the repo alone, both arms pass 100% -> no signal. So the decisive answer MUST NOT be derivable from the repo the agent sees.\n- Obvious regression: do NOT use code smells like 'if false && ...' or commented-out code; a smart agent fixes those without the brain. The regression must be a PLAUSIBLE-BUT-WRONG alternative (a different value, a flipped default, a reordered step) with no visible tell.\n- Answer leakage: the agent must NOT see the correct value/contract anywhere it can read.\n\nTHE RECIPE:\n1. Pick a SPECIFIC decided value or contract in entire-brain that is (a) arbitrary/non-obvious (a real agent can't just guess it), (b) genuinely discussed-with-rationale in the SESSION HISTORY, and (c) checkable by an exact test/grep.\n2. Regression (setup_replacements): change that value/contract to a plausible alternative at base_commit ${BASE}. VERIFY the exact \"old\" string exists in the file at HEAD (read the file).\n3. Scrub the answer + rationale from everything the agent can read: set hide_expected_from_agent:true and hide_validation_from_agent:true, and use setup_commands to strip any README/doc/comment that reveals the correct value or rationale. The ONLY surviving source of the answer must be the session history.\n4. Prompt: SYMPTOM-LEVEL only — describe the regression's symptom and say \"restore the intended/documented behavior from project history\". NEVER state the correct value or name the fix.\n5. validation: commands that all exit 0 only when the EXACT correct state is restored (e.g. 'test $(rg -n \"<exact correct code>\" file | wc -l) -eq 1' plus the focused go test). These are HIDDEN from the agent.\n6. Release hygiene (REQUIRED): conditions [\"no_brain\",\"full_brain\"] (history is the decisive channel; you may also add \"semantic_brain\"); copy_checkpoint_ref_from_source:true; base_commit:\"${BASE}\"; expected_files:[the file]; forbidden_files:[\"go.mod\",\"go.sum\"]; leak_markers:[the focused validation command string]; agent_hidden_paths:[\"benchmarks/agent-brain\"]; prepare_semantic:false unless you need semantic.\n7. brain_queries: SYMPTOM-LEVEL natural language ONLY. The leak auditor FORBIDS: (a) any code-shaped identifier token (length>=4 containing -- prefix, '_', '.', '/', or an internal uppercase letter) that also appears in the hidden answer/validation text; (b) any 3+-word phrase that appears verbatim in hidden text. Two-word natural phrases are fine. So write queries like \"default result count too small\" — NOT \"newQueryCommand\" or \"limit 10\". 3-5 queries.\n\nVERIFY HISTORY HAS THE ANSWER: run the built brain binary to confirm the rationale is genuinely retrievable from this repo's history, e.g.:\n  ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT=${REPO} ${BIN} search \"<your symptom query>\"\n  ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT=${REPO} ${BIN} recall \"<your symptom query>\"\nQuote the strongest hit you find. If history does NOT clearly contain the decision, pick a different anchor.\n\nTEMPLATES to study (read them):\n- ${REPO}/benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entire-brain-history-bundle-sha256.json  (contract-recovery; scrubs docs; hidden validation)\n- ${REPO}/benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entire-brain-query-default-limit.json  (value-recovery; but it is NOT release-clean: it omits hide_validation, leak_markers, agent_hidden_paths and uses identifier brain_queries — you MUST add full hygiene and symptom-level queries).\n\nReturn the complete task JSON as a single valid JSON string (no markdown fences).`\n\nconst anchors = [\n  {\n    label: 'value-recovery',\n    prompt: `${shared}\n\nYOUR ARCHETYPE: VALUE-RECOVERY. Find a non-obvious numeric default/threshold/cap in entire-brain (e.g. a chunk size, confidence threshold, a \"most recent N\" cap, a timeout, a default limit) whose chosen value is arbitrary enough that a smart agent could not reliably guess it, and whose rationale is in history. Regress it to a plausible alternative. id prefix: \"entire-brain-clean-value-\".`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'ordering-bug',\n    prompt: `${shared}\n\nYOUR ARCHETYPE: ORDERING/SEQUENCING BUG. Anchor on this real, history-recorded decision: \"Distill must cache a session fingerprint only AFTER all of that session's chunks succeed; caching before agent success poisoned a real retry by marking 56 failed sessions done after every chunk failed.\" Find the distill fingerprint-caching code (internal/cli/distill*.go) and regress the ORDER so the fingerprint is cached before/regardless of chunk success (a plausible-looking reordering). Validation should be a focused go test proving a failed chunk leaves the session uncached/not-done. Verify the rationale is in history. id prefix: \"entire-brain-clean-order-\".`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'contract-default',\n    prompt: `${shared}\n\nYOUR ARCHETYPE: CONTRACT-DEFAULT. Anchor on a real history-recorded default-behavior decision, e.g.: \"Durable-facts merge/supersede reconciliation is per-chunk and ON by default (accepting ~2x agent-call cost)\" OR \"Regression Radar defaults to precise value-change detection and keeps deletion detection behind opt-in\". Find the code setting that default and regress the DEFAULT to the opposite plausible value. Validation checks the correct default. Verify the rationale is in history. id prefix: \"entire-brain-clean-default-\".`,\n  },\n  {\n    label: 'structured-contract',\n    prompt: `${shared}\n\nYOUR ARCHETYPE: STRUCTURED CONTRACT / OWNERSHIP. Anchor on a real history-recorded structural contract, e.g.: \"seed owns only seed/*, export owns sessions/*; later session exports must NOT delete existing seed files\" OR \"export checkpoint grouping should be based on Git reachability rather than the recorded branch\" OR \"Workspace manifests belong under <plugin-data>/workspaces/, not <plugin-data>/repos/workspaces/\". Find the implementing code and regress it to a plausible alternative that violates the contract. Validation checks the contract holds. Verify the rationale is in history. id prefix: \"entire-brain-clean-contract-\".`,\n  },\n]\n\nconst SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object',\n  additionalProperties: false,\n  required: ['task_id', 'task_json', 'anchor', 'regression_summary', 'why_no_brain_fails', 'why_brain_passes', 'history_evidence', 'old_string_verified_at_head', 'confidence'],\n  properties: {\n    task_id: { type: 'string' },\n    task_json: { type: 'string', description: 'the complete task JSON as a valid JSON string' },\n    anchor: { type: 'string' },\n    regression_summary: { type: 'string' },\n    why_no_brain_fails: { type: 'string' },\n    why_brain_passes: { type: 'string' },\n    history_evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'strongest retrieval hit proving the decision is in history' },\n    old_string_verified_at_head: { type: 'boolean' },\n    confidence: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },\n  },\n}\n\nconst drafts = await parallel(anchors.map(a => () => agent(a.prompt, { label: a.label, phase: 'Author', schema: SCHEMA })))\nreturn drafts.filter(Boolean)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3985,"cache_read_input_tokens":399199,"output_tokens":4113,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3985,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4113,"cache_read_input_tokens":399199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3985},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcBAYNXTiHFT6QSTTLm81","type":"assistant","uuid":"dfdccb00-5c35-4c8d-b3bf-872923f60841","timestamp":"2026-06-18T18:03:57.426Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
