{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-06-18T18:13:33.051Z","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wmo82kh36</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wmo82kh36.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Author 4 clean, harder replay-lab tasks (correctness-axis gap) from distinct archetypes, each verified against real entire-brain code + history\" completed</summary>\n<result>[{\"task_id\":\"entire-brain-clean-value-hook-post-failure-min-score\",\"task_json\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"entire-brain-clean-value-hook-post-failure-min-score\\\",\\\"repo\\\":\\\"entire-brain\\\",\\\"repo_path\\\":\\\"entire-brain\\\",\\\"base_commit\\\":\\\"fc65f656615f4623a2370ec7943f8d575714cfe8\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[\\\"no_brain\\\",\\\"full_brain\\\"],\\\"copy_checkpoint_ref_from_source\\\":true,\\\"prepare_semantic\\\":false,\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"Users report that the agent-harness post-failure hook regressed on precision: after a command fails, it now surfaces weakly-related gotcha/closed-negative facts that share only a single generic term with the failure text, instead of staying quiet unless the match is strong. The relevance bar that gates which facts qualify as a real dead end was loosened. Restore the intended relevance bar from project history so the post-failure hook is high-precision again. Do not change the scoring weights or the matching logic, only the gating bar. Run the focused hook tests before finishing.\\\",\\\"setup_replacements\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"internal/cli/hook_cmd.go\\\",\\\"old\\\":\\\"const hookPostFailureMinScore = 40\\\",\\\"new\\\":\\\"const hookPostFailureMinScore = 10\\\"}],\\\"setup_commands\\\":[\\\"perl -0pi -e 's{// hookPostFailureMinScore is the relevance bar for matching a failure against\\\\\\\\n// gotcha/closed-negative facts: 40 requires several strong term hits or a\\\\\\\\n// locus/substring-grade signal \\\\\\\\(term hit = 10, locus overlap = 60, whole-query\\\\\\\\n// substring = 200\\\\\\\\), keeping the post-failure hook high-precision\\\\\\\\.}{// hookPostFailureMinScore is the relevance bar for matching a failure against gotcha/closed-negative facts.}' internal/cli/hook_cmd.go\\\"],\\\"validation\\\":[\\\"test $(rg -n 'const hookPostFailureMinScore = 40' internal/cli/hook_cmd.go | wc -l | tr -d ' ') -eq 1\\\",\\\"go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestHookMatchFailureKindsAndThreshold|TestHookEmitSilentAndBudget'\\\"],\\\"expected_files\\\":[\\\"internal/cli/hook_cmd.go\\\"],\\\"forbidden_files\\\":[\\\"go.mod\\\",\\\"go.sum\\\"],\\\"hide_expected_from_agent\\\":true,\\\"hide_validation_from_agent\\\":true,\\\"leak_markers\\\":[\\\"go test ./internal/cli -run 'TestHookMatchFailureKindsAndThreshold|TestHookEmitSilentAndBudget'\\\",\\\"const hookPostFailureMinScore = 40\\\"],\\\"agent_hidden_paths\\\":[\\\"benchmarks/agent-brain\\\"],\\\"brain_queries\\\":[\\\"post-failure hook surfacing weak unrelated facts\\\",\\\"failure matcher admitting matches that are too weak\\\",\\\"failure moment precision dropped noisy facts\\\",\\\"scoring threshold for gotcha matches on failures\\\"]}\",\"anchor\":\"internal/cli/hook_cmd.go line 40: const hookPostFailureMinScore = 40 — the relevance-bar/min-score that gates whether a gotcha/closed-negative fact qualifies as a real \\\"dead end\\\" match for a failure in the post-failure agent hook. Decided value 40 (vs the scoring grades term-hit=10, locus-overlap=60, whole-query-substring=200). Regressed to 10.\",\"regression_summary\":\"setup_replacements changes `const hookPostFailureMinScore = 40` -&gt; `= 10` at base_commit fc65f656. setup_commands runs a perl scrub that replaces the 4-line rationale comment (which itself names \\\"40\\\", the scoring grades, and the high-precision rationale) with a single neutral one-line comment, so the agent-readable file has zero answer leakage. 40 vs 10 is a plausible-but-wrong alternative (10 = the single-term-hit floor in the documented scoring model), no code-smell tell. Verified in a clean worktree: at regressed value 10 the file compiles and the focused hook tests still pass (they assert behavior via the f:neg fact at score 90 and silence on unrelated failures, both insensitive to a 10-vs-40 bar), so the test only guards the matching plumbing; the decisive gate is the rg literal `const hookPostFailureMinScore = 40` which is count 0 at the regressed state and count 1 once correctly restored. Symptom is genuine: probe showed a single-term failure makes fact f:gotcha score 20, which surfaces at bar 10 but is correctly suppressed at bar 40 — the exact precision regression described in the prompt.\",\"why_no_brain_fails\":\"The decisive value 40 is arbitrary within the scoring model (10/60/200 grades make 10, 20, 30, 60 all plausible bars) and a no_brain agent has no in-repo signal pinning it: the rationale comment is scrubbed, the focused go tests pass at 10/20/30/60 alike (f:neg scores 90, well above any of them; unrelated query scores 0), README/docs/seed contain no mention of the value or \\\"post-failure hook\\\" rationale (grep confirmed only generic uses of \\\"high-precision\\\" and pattern-scoring weights like 0.40), and the prompt only describes the symptom. So a no_brain agent restores SOME plausible precision bar but not exactly 40, and the hidden rg validation `... = 40` returns count 0 -&gt; validation fails (&lt; 100% pass).\",\"why_brain_passes\":\"The decision lives only in session history. The session 20260611T055732Z (where hook_cmd.go was authored) contains, verbatim in a Write tool call, the full comment \\\"...relevance bar for matching a failure against gotcha/closed-negative facts: 40 requires several strong term hits or a locus/substring-grade signal (term hit = 10, locus overlap = 60, whole-query substring = 200), keeping the post-failure hook high-precision.\\\" and `const hookPostFailureMinScore = 40`. All four symptom-level brain_queries retrieve this exact session via the built brain binary, so a full_brain agent reads the intended value 40, restores it, and both the rg literal check and the focused go test pass.\",\"history_evidence\":\"Brain store session sessions/main/20260611T055732Z_claude-code_fc0c6aa0...jsonl contains verbatim: \\\"relevance bar for matching a failure against\\\\n// gotcha/closed-negative facts: 40 requires several strong term hits or a\\\\n// locus/substring-grade signal (term hit = 10, locus overlap = 60, whole-query\\\\n// substring = 200), keeping the post-failure hook high-precision.\\\\nconst hookPostFailureMinScore = 40\\\". The built binary's `search \\\"failure matcher admitting matches that are too weak\\\"` and `search \\\"post-failure hook surfacing weak unrelated facts\\\"` both return [history] hits in this exact session (history:5d146712..., history:3257a174...).\",\"old_string_verified_at_head\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"task_id\":\"entire-brain-clean-order-distill-cache-after-success\",\"task_json\":\"{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"entire-brain-clean-order-distill-cache-after-success\\\",\\n  \\\"repo\\\": \\\"entire-brain\\\",\\n  \\\"repo_path\\\": \\\"entire-brain\\\",\\n  \\\"base_commit\\\": \\\"fc65f656615f4623a2370ec7943f8d575714cfe8\\\",\\n  \\\"conditions\\\": [\\\"no_brain\\\", \\\"full_brain\\\"],\\n  \\\"copy_checkpoint_ref_from_source\\\": true,\\n  \\\"prepare_semantic\\\": false,\\n  \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"Incremental distill is silently dropping work: when a session's agent chunk calls error out, that session still gets written into the on-disk distill cache as if it were finished, so the very next run treats it as up-to-date and never re-attempts it. A failed session must instead remain uncached so a later run retries it. Restore the intended ordering/behavior documented in the project history. Run the focused distill test before finishing.\\\",\\n  \\\"setup_replacements\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/cli/distill_cmd.go\\\",\\n      \\\"old\\\": \\\"\\\\t\\\\tsessionFailed := false\\\\n\\\\t\\\\tfor chunkIdx, chunk := range ps.chunks {\\\",\\n      \\\"new\\\": \\\"\\\\t\\\\tfor chunkIdx, chunk := range ps.chunks {\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/cli/distill_cmd.go\\\",\\n      \\\"old\\\": \\\"\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\twarnings = append(warnings, fmt.Sprintf(\\\\\\\"agent failed on %s:%d: %v\\\\\\\", session.SessionID, chunk.StartLine, runErr))\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tsessionFailed = true\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tfailedChunks++\\\",\\n      \\\"new\\\": \\\"\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\twarnings = append(warnings, fmt.Sprintf(\\\\\\\"agent failed on %s:%d: %v\\\\\\\", session.SessionID, chunk.StartLine, runErr))\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tfailedChunks++\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/cli/distill_cmd.go\\\",\\n      \\\"old\\\": \\\"\\\\t\\\\t// Only cache a session as distilled when every chunk succeeded, so a\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t// session whose agent calls failed is retried on the next run rather\\\\n\\\\t\\\\t// \n... (truncated 21786 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wmo82kh36.output)</result>\n<usage><agent_count>4</agent_count><subagent_tokens>356308</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>217</tool_uses><duration_ms>575612</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
