{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-06-18T18:31:24.741Z","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wsdyji175</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wsdyji175.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Adversarial bugbot-style review of the proof-gap change set: matrix wiring, evidence integrity, docs honesty, methodology validity\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"confirmed\":[{\"title\":\"Committed release-matrix-report.json/.md were NOT regenerated for the new tracks — release:matrix and CI staleness cmp fail right now\",\"severity\":\"blocker\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/release-matrix-report.json (and .md); enforced by mise.toml release:matrix cmp loop and .github/workflows/test.yml:189-197\",\"detail\":\"The change set updated audit_release_matrix.py (now emits 11 rows incl. the new 'large-repo distill extraction-scheduler speedup' track at lines 208-216, plus reworded notes at line 357) and release-matrix/manifest.json, but the committed matrix report was left at the OLD 10-row content. Verified in BOTH the worktree and the git index: committed report has 10 tracks, no 'large-repo distill extraction' track, and notes[1] still reads 'target large-repo distill...'. Running the updated auditor from the repo root produces 11 tracks with the new row and the new 'frontend/hosted-model distill latency...' wording. cmp therefore differs. Reproduced directly: `mise run release:matrix` -&gt; 'retained release matrix report is stale: release-matrix-report.json' (exit 1), and the CI loop at test.yml:189-197 does the same. This fails release:readiness and the release-evidence CI job. (Note: the sibling distill-perf-large lane report DOES reproduce cleanly — `audit_distill_perf.py` output matches committed JSON+MD — so the matrix report is the sole stale artifact.)\",\"suggested_fix\":\"From the repo root run `mise run release:matrix:update` (or `python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py --manifest benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/manifest.json --out-dir benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix`) and commit the regenerated release-matrix-report.json and .md, then re-run `mise run release:matrix` to confirm it exits 0.\",\"verdict\":{\"title\":\"Committed release-matrix-report.json/.md not regenerated for new tracks — release:matrix cmp gate and CI release-evidence job fail\",\"is_real\":true,\"severity\":\"blocker\",\"reason\":\"Confirmed by direct reproduction. The change set updated benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py (diff vs origin/main adds the new `large-repo distill extraction-scheduler speedup` row at lines 199-216, reword the follow-on row to `frontend/hosted-model distill latency and fact quality`, and reword notes[1] at line ~357) and added the `distill_large` report to release-matrix/manifest.json. But benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/release-matrix-report.json and .md were NOT regenerated: `git diff origin/main HEAD` shows zero changes to those two files, and the committed/HEAD content still has 10 rows with `target large-repo/frontend distill performance` and no `large-repo distill extraction` track.\\n\\nReproduced the failure exactly as the gate runs it: ran `python3 audit_release_matrix.py --manifest .../release-matrix/manifest.json --out-dir $tmp --fail-on-flags` (auditor exits 0, all flags pass) and it produces an 11-row report including the new `large-repo distill extraction-scheduler speedup` track. `cmp -s` of the generated vs committed report DIFFERS for BOTH release-matrix-report.json and .md. That cmp is the exact enforcement at mise.toml:464-472 (`retained release matrix report is stale` -&gt; exit 1) and is duplicated in .github/workflows/test.yml:131-134 (generates into $tmp) + :189-197 (cmp loop -&gt; exit 1). So `mise run release:matrix`, `release:readiness`, and the CI release-evidence job all fail right now.\\n\\nI also adversarially checked the sibling lane the finding flagged as clean: running audit_distill_perf.py against distill-perf-large/manifest.json (exit 0) produces JSON+MD that MATCH the committed distill-perf-large reports. So the matrix report is indeed the sole stale artifact, exactly as claimed.\\n\\nFix is correct: from repo root run `mise run release:matrix:update` (mise.toml:476-494, which runs the auditor with --fail-on-flags into a tmp dir then copies release-matrix-report.json/.md into benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/), commit the regenerated .json and .md, then re-run `mise run release:matrix` to confirm exit 0. Files: /Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/release-matrix-report.json and .md (stale); /Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_release_matrix.py (updated emitter); /Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/mise.toml:464-472,476-494; /Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain/.github/workflows/test.yml:131-134,189-197.\"}},{\"title\":\"Large-repo lane's executed agent script (large_command_agent.py) is committed and hash-pinned in the manifest but NOT validated by the auditor\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf-large/manifest.json (executed_agent.sha256) vs benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py:314-335 (DISTILL_PERF_SOURCE_PATHS at lines 22-26)\",\"detail\":\"The large lane actually executed benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf-large/large_command_agent.py (see commands.serial_run --agent-command), and the manifest pins its sha256 in an `executed_agent` block. But audit_distill_perf.py never reads `executed_agent` (grep: 'NOT REFERENCED') and the hardcoded DISTILL_PERF_SOURCE_PATHS only hash-checks the CURRENT-repo lane's distill-perf/local-command-agent.py. So the script that allegedly produced the large-lane timings is unverified — its committed bytes could drift from the pinned sha256 and the audit would still pass. The current-repo lane does not have this gap because its agent file is in the source-path list and is hash-checked. The asymmetry weakens the large lane's provenance chain that the manifest advertises.\",\"suggested_fix\":\"Have audit_distill_perf.py validate the manifest's executed_agent.{path,sha256} (confirm the path is the same --agent-command referenced in commands.*, resolve it under the evidence dir, and assert file_sha256 matches), adding a flag on mismatch — mirroring the source_sha256 validation.\",\"verdict\":{\"title\":\"Large-repo lane's executed agent (large_command_agent.py) is hash-pinned in manifest's executed_agent block but never validated by the auditor\",\"is_real\":true,\"severity\":\"major\",\"reason\":\"Confirmed real and empirically reproduced. The large lane's three runs all execute `--agent-command python3 benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf-large/large_command_agent.py` (manifest.json:36-38, 55-56, 73-74), and the manifest pins that script's bytes in an `executed_agent.{path,sha256}` block (manifest.json:117-121, pin currently matches actual sha256 79661f48...). However audit_distill_perf.py never reads `executed_agent` (grep: NOT REFERENCED), and the hardcoded DISTILL_PERF_SOURCE_PATHS (audit_distill_perf.py:22-26) used by validate_source_hashes (lines 314-335) only hash-checks the CURRENT-repo lane's `distill-perf/local-command-agent.py` — `large_command_agent.py` appears in neither source_sha256 nor artifact_sha256 of the large manifest.\\n\\nDrift test (proves exploitable): appending bytes to large_command_agent.py changed its sha256 to 01864d63... (diverging from the pin), yet `python3 audit_distill_perf.py --manifest .../distill-perf-large/manifest.json --repo-root . --fail-on-flags` still exited 0 (PASS) — the exact invocation CI uses (.github/workflows/test.yml:123-126). I restored the file. The asymmetry the reviewer flagged is correct: the current-repo lane's executed agent (distill-perf/local-command-agent.py, present on disk, 1794 bytes) IS in the hash-checked list and cannot drift undetected; the large lane's cannot make that claim.\\n\\nSeverity = major, not blocker: the gap does not falsify the timing numbers (artifacts dry-run/jobs-1/jobs-4 and the four distill source files plus audit script are still hash-checked, and the 2.2x speedup math is independent of the agent bytes). It is a provenance-integrity hole in an audit lane whose entire purpose is tamper-evidence: the manifest advertises an `executed_agent` p\n... (truncated 121778 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wsdyji175.output)</result>\n<usage><agent_count>22</agent_count><subagent_tokens>1263954</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>392</tool_uses><duration_ms>830274</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
