{"parentUuid":"48152b03-1be1-476b-b89a-06915b71b82f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01TWvQ55bdyPjf81Bj21j8rk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**What I'm waiting on (the only blocker):** the P0.1 proof run — real Codex agent runs at n=4 on the two genuine candidates. It can't be faked or sped up; producing fabricated lift numbers is exactly what this repo's evidence discipline forbids. ETA ~30–60 min.\n\n**Everything else is done or finalizing in parallel:**\n- **P0.2 (large-repo distill timing): fully complete + hardened** — auditor-clean, wired into matrix/mise/CI/press release, and the 4 confirmed bugbot findings on it are fixed + verified (matrix regen, executed_agent tamper-evidence, reconcile equality, contract-task greps).\n- **Loop-audit:** a focused re-review of those fixes is running now (Claude, no contention with the Codex run).\n\n**The honest P0.1 picture from the completed pilot:** of the 4 authored clean tasks, only **fact-merge** shows a clean correctness gap (brain 2/2, no_brain 1/2); `order-cache` saturated (no_brain solves from the symptom), `value-hook` the brain raised quality (94 vs 71) but didn't recover the exact value, and `contract` needed the validation fix it now has. The n=4 run will tell me whether fact-merge (+ contract) **genuinely flips `proof_ready`**. If it does, I register it as a real proof; if not, I deliver the honest negative — the brain helps directionally but a stable proof-ready lift against gpt-5.5 isn't there yet. I'll finalize the verdict the moment the run lands."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5441,"cache_read_input_tokens":544466,"output_tokens":1246,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5441,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available",