{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-06-18T19:09:30.559Z","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wjwgvj740</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wjwgvj740.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Re-verify the fixes applied after the first adversarial review introduced no new defects and resolved the confirmed findings\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"confirmed_real\":[{\"title\":\"Reused Ollama go-test contract artifact names test functions that no longer exist in the tree\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf-large/go-test-internal-cli-ollama-distill.jsonl (and ../distill-perf/ shared copy); manifest.json:84-115\",\"detail\":\"The shared loopback-Ollama go-test JSONL (sha bc511ffa..., source_head 848909cb) certifies TestExecOllamaDistillAgent*/TestLoopbackOnlyDialContext* etc. The new README explicitly documents that those named test functions have since been removed from the tree (the underlying functionality in distill_cmd.go remains) and that the auditor validates the retained artifact rather than live code, so the gate is unaffected. This is a pre-existing property of the current-repo lane's artifact, reused verbatim here (cmp confirms identical bytes), not introduced by this change.\",\"is_real\":true,\"reason\":\"It is a genuine staleness: the retained contract pins test names absent from HEAD. Severity is minor because (a) it pre-exists on origin/main in the distill-perf lane, (b) the README transparently flags it as release-hardening follow-up, and (c) it does not affect the auditor gate, which checks the retained artifact's recorded pass results, not live tests.\"}],\"all\":[{\"title\":\"Fix verified: validate_executed_agent() correctly handles path-traversal, optional-field, and binding cases\",\"severity\":\"nit\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py:338-373\",\"detail\":\"Ran 12 adversarial cases against the function: None block -&gt; (None, []) (current-repo lane unaffected); non-dict -&gt; flagged; foo/../path and absolute /etc/passwd -&gt; rejected by `rel.is_absolute() or '..' in rel.parts`; empty/missing path -&gt; flagged; bad sha format -&gt; flagged; missing file -&gt; flagged; sha mismatch -&gt; flagged but still returns the on-disk actual hash (consistent with validate_local_ollama_contract); binding miss (`path not in tokens`) -&gt; flagged per command; full valid case -&gt; clean. The function is invoked at line 403 and feeds the new `executed_agent` report field at line 508. All correct.\",\"is_real\":false,\"reason\":\"This is a confirmation that the fix is correct, not a defect. Every guard behaves as intended; the current-repo lane (no executed_agent key) is genuinely unaffected and reports executed_agent: null with status pass.\"},{\"title\":\"Binding check is membership-only, not bound to --agent-command position\",\"severity\":\"nit\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py:369-372\",\"detail\":\"The check is `if isinstance(tokens, list) and path not in tokens`. It verifies the executed_agent.path string appears somewhere in the command token array, but does not assert it is the value following an `--agent-command` flag. A crafted manifest could place the path as an unrelated token and still pass the binding gate. In the real large-repo manifest the path is correctly the value after `--agent-command` in all three commands, and validate_command separately enforces `--agent command`, so the actual evidence binds legitimately. A `./`-prefixed path would also pass file resolution but would fail the membership check unless the tokens use the identical `./` form (so it is fail-safe, not fail-open, for that variant).\",\"is_real\":false,\"reason\":\"Not a defect introduced by this fix and not exploitable in the retained evidence. The membership check is a reasonable tamper-evidence floor; tightening it to require adjacency with --agent-command would be a hardening nicety, not a correctness bug. No false pass occurs on the committed manifests.\"},{\"title\":\"Adding reconcile_agent_calls/total_agent_calls to comparable_fields does not break either lane\",\"severity\":\"nit\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/audit_distill_perf.py:484-487\",\"detail\":\"Verified both lanes have equal serial/parallel values for the two new fields: current-repo serial/parallel reconcile=150/150, total=335/335; large-repo reconcile=545/545, total=1383/1383. If a field were missing in one artifact the mismatch fires; if missing in both, the dedicated checks at L456-459 (extraction_agent_calls must be positive; total_agent_calls must equal extraction+reconcile) still guard. No silent pass.\",\"is_real\":false,\"reason\":\"Confirmation the comparable_fields change is safe. No regression; both lanes pass.\"},{\"title\":\"Cascade is internally consistent: sha updates + regenerated reports verified\",\"severity\":\"nit\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf/manifest.json:24; benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/distill-perf-large/manifest.json:24,117-121\",\"detail\":\"Recomputed hashes: audit_distill_perf.py actual = sha256:fb0de70c... matches source_sha256 entry in BOTH manifests; large_command_agent.py actual = sha256:79661f48... matches executed_agent.sha256. Ran the auditor on both manifests with --repo-root . --fail-on-flags: both PASS, EXIT 0, 6/6 source hashes, current-repo speedup 3.16x&gt;=1.25, large-repo 2.22x&gt;=1.5. Regenerated JSON and MD reports for both lanes and the release-matrix byte-match the committed reports (manifest path field normalized). release-matrix auditor passes with 0 flags; press release contains the new 'frontend/hosted-model distill' guardrail and no longer the old 'target large-repo/frontend distill' string.\",\"is_real\":false,\"reason\":\"Confirmation, not a defect. The full cascade (two distill manifests + release-matrix manifest/auditor + press release) is internally consistent and reproducible.\"},{\"title\":\"Release-matrix and both distill reports regenerate byte-identical (no cmp-staleness)\",\"severity\":\"nit\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release-matrix/release-matrix-report.{json,md}; evidence/distill-perf/distill-perf-audit-report.{json,md}; evidence/distill-perf-large/distill-perf-audit-report.{json,md}\",\"detail\":\"Regenerated all three via audit_release_matrix.py and audit_distill_perf.py into temp dirs and cmp -s against the committed copies: all six files MATCH byte-for-byte, matrix RC=0 with 0 flags. The current-repo distill report's only diff (added \\\"executed_agent\\\": null) reproduces exactly because the current-repo manifest has no executed_agent block.\",\"is_real\":false,\"reason\":\"Confirmed not a defect — the committed reports are fresh and match regeneration exactly.\"},{\"title\":\"Contract-checkpoint behavioral-only validation fails-as-expected on regression and passes when fixed\",\"severity\":\"nit\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entire-brain-clean-contract-checkpoint-branch-reachability.json:23-30\",\"detail\":\"In a detached worktree at HEAD (== base_commit fc65f656), I applied the setup_replacement (reorders BranchesFor so metadataBranch wins over default-branch reachability), ran the perl test-removal, materialized zz_contract_validation_test.go, and ran the injected TestReachableCheckpointRoutesToDefaultBranchFolder: it FAILS on the regression (session lands under feature/already-merged instead of main) and PASSES after restoring the fix. Critically, in the regressed state ONLY this injected test fails across the whole ./internal/cli package (Export|Checkpoint|Branch|SelectedSession all pass, package compiles, go vet clean) — so dropping the byte-exact greps is sound: the behavioral test is the sole discriminator and no other retained test catches the regression for free.\",\"is_real\":false,\"reason\":\"The edit to rely only on the injected behavioral test is correct and verified end-to-end.\"},{\"title\":\"Two value-recovery tasks rely on byte-exact rg greps, not behavioral tests, to detect the regression\",\"severity\":\"nit\",\"location\":\"benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entire-brain-clean-default-fact-merge-confidence.json:24-25; entire-brain-clean-value-hook-post-failure-min-score.json:24-25\",\"detail\":\"Empirically, in the regressed state the behavioral go test (2nd validation command) PASSES for both default-fact-merge (0.75-&gt;0.70) and value-hook (40-&gt;10); only the rg grep for the exact answer string catches the regression. This is b\n... (truncated 7412 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-Documents-Coding-entire-brain/4e09703c-666f-441f-9b82-52efaa7da599/tasks/wjwgvj740.output)</result>\n<usage><agent_count>2</agent_count><subagent_tokens>182001</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>83</tool_uses><duration_ms>512740</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
