{"parentUuid":"a619e502-d86e-44af-8cb9-56a42f56e7ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0147JVeosWnkDyyak94sJGZe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed running (in tool/brain-prep before the first Codex call — normal). \n\n**Status — what's left is one clean run:**\n\nThe earlier proof run was invalid — I'd carelessly left review workflows running subagents (building worktrees, running `go test`/auditors) *concurrently* with the Codex proof run, which starved/contaminated it (every run showed `changed_files=0`, uniform-fail). That's on me. I've cleaned it up and relaunched a **clean, isolated** run (panel `p01-clean-proof`: fact-merge + contract, n=4) with **nothing else running**.\n\n- **ETA: ~30–50 min** (16 real Codex agent runs — can't be compressed without faking, which the evidence discipline forbids).\n- **Verdict it produces:** fact-merge is the one candidate with a clean gap in the trustworthy pilot (brain 2/2, no_brain 1/2). If it holds at n=4 (brain 4/4, no_brain <4/4, drop-one survives) → **genuine `proof_ready` flip → I register it** (flip the release-lane claim policy, regenerate audits, ledger row). If not → **honest negative**: the brain helps directionally but a stable proof-ready lift against gpt-5.5 isn't there — itself a real, ledger-worthy finding (and exactly why this is \"the single thing between useful and proven\").\n\n**Everything else is finished:** P0.2 (large-repo distill timing) complete, hardened, and bugbot-re-reviewed clean; the loop-audit fixes are verified. Nothing pushed — I'll have the full diff + the verdict ready for your review.\n\nI'll deliver the final result the moment this clean run lands."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1600,"cache_read_input_tokens":573413,"output_tokens":1181,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier"