annot guess the\n  exact arbitrary value; the focused go test passes at several plausible values,\n  so the hidden exact-value check is the sole discriminator.\n- **full_brain recovers it from history and passes — 4/4.** The history channel\n  surfaces the decided value with its rationale; the agent restores it exactly.\n\nThis is a stable `brain_positive` comparison (pass-rate lift surviving the\ndrop-one robustness check at n=4), so `proof_ready=true`.\n\n## Scope — what this does NOT claim\n\nThis lane claims agent lift **only for the history channel, correctness axis,\nwith `claude:sonnet:high`.** It does **not** claim:\n\n- MCP, Radar, semantic, or workspace agent lift, or\n- codex-runner agent lift, or\n- a token/efficiency win.\n\nThose remain `no_release_claim` in `../release` (the B1 clean reruns are\naudit-clean but not proof-ready). The co-located contract-checkpoint comparison\n**saturated** (Sonnet solves it without the brain) and is retained as an honest\nnon-proof-ready datapoint.\n\n## Provenance / why this is a separate lane\n\nThe codex `gpt-5.5` workspace ran out of credits during the proof attempt, so\nthe n=4 confirmation was run with the Claude runner (post-limit-reset). The\nrelease lane (`../release`) is codex-based and stays `no_release_claim` for the\nmcp/radar scopes it still cannot prove; this lane is the honest home for the one\nscope that is now proven. Records are redacted of host paths and contributor\nnames; the suite directory name matches each record's\n`provenance.run_config.suite` so the panel-provenance integrity check passes.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aeda6bde-c935-4100-9cbf-7b691b982552","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"92025ff4-9893-472f-a9f3-e3074e744231","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"64","subject":"P0.2 offline: large-repo distill timing on entireio/cli","description":"Run `distill --dry-run --json` (offline) on the entireio/cli large corpus (822 sessions / 1.6G) for real large-repo sizing, plus paired timed --jobs 1 vs --jobs N via --agent command + local-command-agent (deterministic, no model) on a temp brain copy. Produces dry-run.json/jobs-1.json/jobs-N.json with matching cache/timing fields. No hosted-model usage.","activeForm":"Running offline large-repo distill timing","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"65","subject":"P0.2: build distill-perf manifest + pass audit_distill_perf.py","description":"Author a new evidence manifest with a target block for github.com/entireio/cli and widened claim_scope (large-repo command-agent scheduler speedup), retain artifacts + go-test ollama contract, run audit_distill_perf.py to PASS. Then update press release Proven/Pending lines + eval_ledger row + regenerate release-matrix distill track. Honest scope: command-agent measures scheduler parallelism; note hosted-model latency is separate.","activeForm":"Building distill-perf manifest and passing the auditor","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"66","subject":"P0.1 author: harder/clean correctness-axis replay-lab tasks","description":"Author 3-5 candidate tasks where the decisive answer lives in the brain (history rationale / durable fact / semantic locator) and is NOT recoverable from the repo in budget, so no_brain fails (<100%) and brain reliably passes (100%) → clean correctness_win at n>=4. Symptom-level brain_queries (pass brain_query_leak_audit), hide validation+expected, leak_markers + agent_hidden_paths, pinned base_commit. Templates from existing tasks/*.json.","activeForm":"Authoring harder/clean replay-lab tasks","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"67","subject":"P0.1 offline-validate: leak-audit clean + fails-as-expected + panel","description":"For each candidate task: run `run.py check` (offline, no model) to confirm the regression fails-as-expected, and confirm brain_query_leak_audit passes (no answer-bearing identifiers/phrases). Iterate JSON until clean. Build a panel JSON sized for n>=4-8/side. All offline — no hosted-model usage.","activeForm":"Offline-validating tasks (leak-audit + fails-as-expected)","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"68","subject":"P0.1 (post-2PM): run pilots → scale n>=4-8 → check proof_ready","description":"Codex gpt-5.5 ran out of credits after the pilot. Pilot (trustworthy) showed fact-merge brain 2/2 vs no_brain 1/2 (directional lift); order-cache saturated; value-hook brain raised quality but missed exact value. User authorized a Claude-runner proof. Now running clean isolated panel p01-clean-proof-claude (claude:sonnet:high, fact-merge+contract, n=4) for the definitive proof_ready verdict.","activeForm":"Running pilots and scaling to proof-ready n","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"69","subject":"P0.1 (post-2PM): register genuine proofs or honest negative","description":"If a suite genuinely flips proof_ready: copy into evidence/release/ matching release_citable_suite_globs, flip manifest claim_policy no_release_claim→proof_required with required_proof_scopes, regenerate codex-audit + release-matrix reports, add eval_ledger row, update press release. If it does NOT flip: document the honest negative finding + what was learned. NEVER fabricate numbers.","activeForm":"Registering genuine proofs (or honest negative)","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"70","subject":"Loop-audit until clean (bugbot-proof)","description":"go build/vet/test/gofmt clean; run full `mise run release:readiness` (all auditors + cmp staleness) green; adversarial self-review workflow over new tasks/manifests/docs for leakage, provenance gaps, stale reports, doc-claim mismatches, schema typos, no person-names; loop until dry. Review-before-push (do not push without user review).","activeForm":"Loop-auditing until no issues remain","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"71","subject":"P0.2 wiring: matrix track + mise + CI + press release + ledger","description":"Wire the large-repo distill lane: make audit_release_matrix.py \"target large-repo distill\" track read the new report and flip to proven (scoped to command-agent scheduler speedup at scale); add reports.distill_large to the release-matrix manifest; add mise distill:large:evidence(+:update) into release:readiness; add CI auditor+cmp; update press release Proven/Pending lines; add eval_ledger row. Flag the stale ollama-contract (tests removed from code) finding.","activeForm":"Wiring the large-repo distill lane into matrix/mise/CI/docs","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":8},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5a85f124-c454-4d47-b27a-feb730f8a9c8","timestamp":"2026-06-18T21:26:10.893Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain","sessionId":"af861ed9-9e1d-41a7-8400-b53c2995aed8","version":"2.1.177","gitBranch":"claude/proof-gap-replay-distill","slug":"zippy-floating-lovelace"}
